eir cookies; receipts\n   147\tcan land >12 s later. \"Browser\"/\"stranger\" checks without a bot (D06, D09) = send the Sec-Fetch-* + Referer/Origin\n   148\tmatrix yourself. NEW CLASS = write lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit (D11\n   149\tdid -> TT first try; D09, D10, D12, D13, D15 TT went solver_incomplete). Banners are costume; the title pun names the bug.\n   150\t```\n   151\t\n   152\t## Readiness gaps\n   153\t\n   154\tPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (~6-9 lane-days at the current pace). \"prebuild\" = pure python handler\n   155\t(request planner + response parser, no I/O; the solver fetches) with offline fixtures = recorded bodies incl. a\n   156\tdecoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built (no web prebuild lane, no `web:*` keys in\n   157\t.run/prebuild-state.json). Dropped after D13: `ssti-engine-probe` (seen D11), `port-day22-handlers`. Dropped after\n   158\tD15: `ssrf-planner` (seen D15; replaced by `ssrf-filter-bypass`); D14's inventory field x action read folded into\n   159\t`bopla-field-read` (now the no-inventory sibling). Added after D15: `ssrf-filter-bypass`, `api-shadow-version`,\n   160\t`api-resource-limit-overread`, `api-unsafe-consumption`.\n   161\t\n   162\t```json\n   163\t[\n   164\t  {\"id\": \"enable-web-prebuild-lane\", \"concept\": \"harness: web is not a prebuild lane\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Still true after D15 (hctf/prebuild.py has no `web` string at all): hctf/prebuild.py LANES has no `web` entry (AUTO_LANES lists 5 lanes) and .run/prebuild-state.json has no web:* keys, so no prebuild gap below can drain. lib/web/handlers/ already loads per-day p\n   165\t  {\"id\": \"codify-before-tt\", \"concept\": \"harness: the class handler must exist before Time Trial starts\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D15 repeated it: Fetch Quest TT started 13:18:04Z, ~5 s after single CORRECT, and the codify worker's lib/web/handlers/day24_web_fetch_quest.py landed ~1 min later -> TT solver_incomplete 41 s, live worker hand-solved. Same on D12/D13 (41 s, 1\n   166\t  {\"id\": \"cmd-injection-planner\", \"concept\": \"OS command injection to read the mounted proof (row 10)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For each flagged param (host, ip, target, domain, filename, cmd): separators ; | || && %0a $() backticks, with/without a valid prefix (127.0.0.1), reading the prompt path (default /run/huntress/objective.txt) via cat, `$(cat ...)` echoed, `$\n   167\t  {\"id\": \"xxe-payloads\", \"concept\": \"XML external entities (row 18)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"XML endpoints/uploads: in-band entity on the prompt path, parameter-entity variant, php://filter base64, XInclude, SVG / DOCX (zipfile) container builder carrying the entity. Parser: proof regex, base64 decode. D10 proved an upload kit with `upload_shape: POST JSON filename/\n   168\t  {\"id\": \"jwt-session-forge\", \"concept\": \"JWT alg:none / leaked-secret HS256 / Flask-itsdangerous / Express s: cookies (rows 7, 8)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Session family opened on D08. Pure python (hmac, hashlib, base64, json, zlib): decode JWT; produce alg none ('none'/'None'/'NONE', empty sig), HS256 re-signed with secrets FOUND in recon (clues, backups, .env, JS\n   169\t  {\"id\": \"role-tamper-planner\", \"concept\": \"client-controlled role: header / query / cookie / claim (row 6; body binding seen D13)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every clue JSON (still on D14/D15) shows current_role: analyst; D13 granted admin via JSON body binding (mass assignment, seen) -- the sibling forms are untested. From recon: role field and values (current_role, \n   170\t  {\"id\": \"open-redirect-planner\", \"concept\": \"open redirect / OAuth redirect_uri (row 24b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Params next, return, returnTo, redirect, url, continue, redirect_uri, callback on login/logout/OAuth routes. Payloads: //evil, /\\\\evil, https:evil, %2F%2Fevil, /%09/evil, https://<base>@evil, javascript: (if the sink is client-side), plus the clue rout\n   171\t  {\"id\": \"dom-xss-sink-scan\", \"concept\": \"DOM XSS: client-side source -> sink (row 13c)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Third XSS flavour after D06 reflected / D07 stored. Static scan of inline and linked JS for sources (location.hash/search/href, document.referrer, postMessage data, localStorage) flowing into sinks (innerHTML, outerHTML, insertAdjacentHTML, document.write\n   172\t  {\"id\": \"clue-json-router\", \"concept\": \"map /api/clues keys + bare-route JSON errors + prompt verbs to the concept and the next request\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every target since D05 serves /api/clues {framework, feature_route, secondary_route, current_role, <concept key>}. Pure function: clues JSON (+ bare-route error bodies) -> concept + request plan. Known keys\n   173\t  {\"id\": \"mastery-concept-dispatcher\", \"concept\": \"run every known lane concept on every target without recursion or starvation\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 Mastery (3 targets) took ~15 min: racing every earlier solver on every target slowed the app 5 s -> 13 s, and day-21 solvers' fallback() imported each other (infinite recursion). Registry in lib/web/ (package; s\n   174\t  {\"id\": \"recon-crawl-depth2\", \"concept\": \"shared recon planner: robots/sitemap/openapi/comments/clue JSON/links, depth 2 (rows 1, 5, 22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Given fetched bodies keyed by path, return next same-origin GETs: robots Allow/Disallow, sitemap <loc>, openapi.json `paths` (fill {id} from submit responses), href/src/action, fetch('/..') literals, HTML-\n   175\t  {\"id\": \"fetch-metadata-matrix\", \"concept\": \"server-judged 'browser' checks: Sec-Fetch-* / Referer / Origin matrix (rows 13a, 24a, 15)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D06 (same-origin callback) and D09 (cross-site CSRF) were both judged purely by request headers, no bot. Pure planner: given a route, a base URL and an optional 'from' page URL, emit header sets {Sec-Fetch-S\n   176\t  {\"id\": \"record-target-responses\", \"concept\": \"replayable live-target cases\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Targets 410 after CORRECT; D07 Mastery's proof-2 fix could only be tested on a hand-built mock. Harness: log every target request/response during single/TT/Mastery into solver/cases/<case>/http/ and let solve.py replay them when the host 410s; also the fixture source fo\n   177\t  {\"id\": \"stopgate-503-already-solved\", \"concept\": \"harness: a 503 submit that landed leaves the stop gate closed\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D07 Mastery: submit returned HTTP 503 temporarily_unavailable though the GM registered CORRECT; the retry returned already_solved and stop_gate.py (counts only accepted/correct rows) never released. Owner of hctf/: after a 503, check\n   178\t  {\"id\": \"prototype-pollution\", \"concept\": \"server-side prototype pollution (row 25)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Node-flavoured JSON merge/settings routes: {\\\"__proto__\\\":{\\\"isAdmin\\\":true,\\\"role\\\":\\\"admin\\\"}}, {\\\"constructor\\\":{\\\"prototype\\\":{...}}}, query-string a[__proto__][x]=1; then re-request the clue/status route. Detect via a reflected polluted key (e.g. json s\n   179\t  {\"id\": \"ssrf-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"SSRF sequels: filtered host/scheme, redirect, file://, blind (row 12b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D15 was the plain form (feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<internal_only route>; port 80 -> fetch_failed). Sequels in the D10->D11 / D03->D12 style: blocklist on 127.0.0.1/localhost -> 2130706433, 0x7f000001, 017700000001, 127.1, \n   180\t  {\"id\": \"api-shadow-version\", \"concept\": \"improper API inventory: shadow / deprecated / beta endpoint skips the check (row 39, OWASP API9)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D13-D15 walked the OWASP API Top 10 (API3, API5, API7) and D14's prompt said 'take inventory of every endpoint'. Planner: from /api/inventory, /openapi.json, /swagger.json, /api-docs, /v2/api-docs, /api/\n   181\t  {\"id\": \"nosql-operator-injection\", \"concept\": \"MongoDB-style operator injection (row 19)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"JSON bodies: {\\\"$ne\\\":null}, {\\\"$gt\\\":\\\"\\\"}, {\\\"$regex\\\":\\\".*\\\"}; form username[$ne]=x; $where only when Mongo-flavoured. Field names from the form/JS. Parser: proof or an admin page with the returned session.\"},\n   182\t  {\"id\": \"deserialization-gadgets\", \"concept\": \"pickle / PHP / node-serialize cookies (row 21)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Recognise base64 cookies gASV/gAN (pickle), Tzo/YTo (PHP), {\\\"rce\\\" / _$$ND_FUNC$$_ (node-serialize), rO0 (Java). Prefer data tampering (isAdmin/role) over code execution; minimal gadget reading the prompt path otherwise.\"},\n   183\t  {\"id\": \"ssti-sandbox-escape\", \"concept\": \"SSTI sequels: filtered/sandboxed engine, file read, stored template (row 11b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D11 rendered `{{objective}}` directly (context var) under a Spring Boot costume; `{{T(java.lang.Runtime)}}` printed a class, ${..}/*{..} stayed lite","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/2f22de87-85c6-4735-9cd3-ecbd50af08de/tool-results/bdd3oyqei.txt","persistedOutputSize":36798},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01575bepukbBVKtmxp7g9wg5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reas