me. Success = proof regex, never `effect` alone (D12 empty rows; D16's harmless baseline already says\n`worker_command_completed`). Any file read shows `/run/huntress/config.json` whose `weakness` names the class.\nMastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days (4 targets since D15), described only by today's prompt.\nPace: D01-D03 cal. 19, D04-D05 cal. 20, D06-D08 cal. 21, D09-D10 cal. 22, D11-D13 cal. 23, D14-D15 cal. 24, D16-D18\ncal. 25 -> D19-D31 (13 lane-days) over cal. 26-31, ~2-3 per day; priority 1 below = likely in D19-D27.\nArc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read -> XSS (reflected, stored) -> session -> CSRF ->\nupload -> SSTI -> second-order SQLi -> OWASP API run (API3/API5 mass assignment + field/action authz, API7 SSRF) ->\nOS command injection -> authentication flow (API2: reset) -> GraphQL (same `protected_reference`/case/note shape as\nD14 behind a resolver). Sequels are common (D10->D11, D03->D12, D05->D13->D14, D14->D18). D18's prompt (\"vary the\nprotocol surface without changing the underlying authorization discipline\") and D17's multi-step flow point at:\nmore auth-flow bugs (JWT/session forgery, MFA/OTP step skip, OAuth redirect_uri), other API surfaces (WebSocket,\nbatched/aliased GraphQL, version-swapped REST), and the untouched classics (XXE, DOM XSS, open redirect, prototype\npollution, NoSQL, deserialization, race, CORS, header trust, CRLF, cache poisoning).\nSnapshot 2026-10-25 (after D18). `lib/web/handlers/__init__.py` holds `session_fixation`, `upload`, `csrf` (+\n`default` ladder) and loads per-day plugins `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS): D23 SSTI,\nsecond-order, mass assignment; D24 field/action authz, SSRF; D25 `day25_web_shell_company` (KEY\n`example_path|input_parameter|command|shell|exec`), `day25_web_reset_expectations` (KEY `recovery_guide_route|..`),\n`day25_web_resolver_revolt` (KEY `protected_reference|resolver|graphql|..`, overlaps D14's key -> both race).\n`hctf prebuild` still has 