{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgP1cwhFVVbyFgxjZ6BwN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WRuvLqBFbdBzv9MvGq5MW7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/web.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('## Readiness gaps'); a=s.index('```json',i); b=s.index('```',a+7)\ngaps=json.loads(s[a+7:b])\nG={g['id']:g for g in gaps}\nfor d in ('cmd-injection-planner','graphql-introspection'): G.pop(d)\nG['enable-web-prebuild-lane']['detail']=G['enable-web-prebuild-lane']['detail'].replace('Still true after D15','Still true after D18 (D25 added three more per-day plugins by hand)')\nG['codify-before-tt']['detail']=(\"D16-D18 (cal. 25) repeated it three times at once: singles CORRECT in ~36-40 s at 13:01:01-07Z, codify plugins landed 13:01:08-10Z, TT started 13:01:10Z -> all three TT solver_incomplete (13.8-22 s), hand-solved by live workers in 31-53 s; the D16 plugin was still a `.tmp` when its Mastery ran (3/4 answered, proof-4 hand-solved). Earlier: D09, D10, D12, D13, D15. D11 (plugin before submit) and D14 went first try. \"\n  \"Owner of hctf/ + web skill: for web, gate TT/Mastery start on the codify worker's plugin being importable (or on solver-test passing the single case), and have the single worker write the plugin (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS, generic over param/field/route words) before `hctf submit` -- with ~40 s singles the plugin is now the long pole.\")\nG['clue-json-router']['detail']+=(\" D16: input_parameter + example_path (400 path_required) -> cmd injection, value = example + %3B + `cat /run/huntress/objective.txt` (plugin day25_web_shell_company.py). D17: recovery_guide_route -> guide JSON {request_route, redeem_route, account_parameter, token_parameter, accounts[{id,self_service}]} -> own token redeemed with the victim id (day25_web_reset_expectations.py). D18: protected_reference + note + current_user (no framework key), feature GET 404 not_found -> GraphQL introspection + case(id) (day25_web_resolver_revolt.py). KEY collision: protected_reference is D14 (with inventory_route) AND D18 (with note) -> route on the companion key; and any `*_guide_route`/`inventory_route` value is a JSON map of the next requests.\")\nG['logic-race-reset']['concept']='business logic and race conditions (row 26; reset tokens seen D17 -> sequels in auth-flow gap)'\nG['logic-race-reset']['detail']=(\"D17 opened multi-step flows (request -> redeem). Remaining: numeric fields (negative, zero, huge, float), coupon/redeem replay, ~20-request parallel burst for a single-use action (redeem, transfer, vote), step reordering in a checkout/approval flow. Read every guide/inventory JSON for the steps. No credential guessing. Parser: proof regex.\")\nG['logic-race-reset']['priority']=1\nG['nosql-operator-injection']['priority']=1\nG['deserialization-gadgets']['priority']=1\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"runtime-config-oracle\",\"concept\":\"/run/huntress/config.json names the weakness once any file read works\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"D16's `cat /run/huntress/*` printed config.json {schema: huntress.web_exploitation.runtime_config.v1, profile_id: framework_<lang>_<fw>_<weakness>, framework_cell, weakness: os_command_injection, mode: single|time_trial|mastery, layout...} next to objective.txt. Owner of lib/web: after any handler achieves a file read (LFI D04, cmd D16, SSTI file read, XXE, SSRF file://), also read /run/huntress/config.json and log `weakness`/`profile_id` -- a free classifier for unknown Mastery targets and for the codify worker's KEY_MAP. Never submit anything from it; the proof is still objective.txt.\"},\n {\"id\":\"mfa-step-skip-auth-flow\",\"concept\":\"auth-flow sequels: MFA/OTP step skip, Host-header reset link, leaked/reused codes, login state machine (row 27b)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D17 (reset token not bound to account) was the first authentication-flow day (OWASP API2). Planner over a guide/clue JSON or form chain: identify steps (login -> otp/verify -> session; request -> email/preview -> redeem); try calling the final step with the step-1 state (cookie/token) and no code, an empty/null/array code, the code issued to OUR account on another account_id/username, a code echoed in any response, a step-2 response flag (`mfa_required:false`, `verified:true`) set in the JSON body; reset links built from X-Forwarded-Host / Host to a route we can read. Parameter names from the guide (`account_parameter`, `token_parameter`, `code`, `otp`). Parser: proof regex / evidence. No brute force of codes.\"},\n {\"id\":\"websocket-authz\",\"concept\":\"WebSocket / alternate transport skips the REST authz (row 41)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D18's prompt: 'Vary the protocol surface without changing the underlying authorization discipline' -- the same protected object reached via another transport. Planner: find ws:// / wss:// / socket.io / SSE / JSON-RPC endpoints in inline JS and clues; build the handshake (Origin same/foreign/null for CSWSH) and send the protected read (protected_reference) as a message; also JSON-RPC {method, params} over POST and REST<->GraphQL equivalents of the same op. Pure planner emits frames; the solver needs a minimal RFC6455 client (stdlib socket+ssl, masking) -- add it to lib/websolve if absent. Parser: proof regex over frames.\"},\n {\"id\":\"cmd-injection-sequels\",\"concept\":\"command injection sequels: filtered separators, blind, argument injection (row 10b)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D16 was the plain form (`ls -ld <path>` with stdout echoed; `;` worked once percent-encoded). Sequel planner, input = param name (input_parameter / `<x>_required`) + example value: separators %3B, %0a, %26%26, %7C, $(..), backticks, ${IFS} for spaces, quotes-split (c''at), wildcard paths (/run/hunt*/obj*); argument injection when the value is an argument not a shell string (`--output=/app/static/x`, `-exec cat {} ;` for find, `--help`-style); blind: copy the proof into a served static dir (the example path, e.g. /app/static) then GET it. Parser: proof regex in stdout/body or in the copied file.\"},\n {\"id\":\"graphql-batch-alias-mutation\",\"concept\":\"GraphQL sequels: aliases, batched arrays, mutations without authz, introspection off (row 23b)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D18 was the plain form (introspection on, one resolver skipped the field check). Sequel planner from the schema: alias the protected field across every arg-taking Query field (a1:case(id:..){..} a2:...), JSON array batching [{query},{query}], mutations (updateX/setRole/assign) reachable without authz followed by the read, node(id:)/Relay global ids (base64 'Type:id'), fragments on interfaces/unions to reach hidden types; introspection disabled -> field-suggestion walk ('Did you mean') and common names (note, secret, proof, evidence, internal). Transports: POST JSON, GET ?query=, form, application/graphql body. Parser: proof regex over data and errors[].message.\"},\n {\"id\":\"crlf-header-injection\",\"concept\":\"CRLF / response-header injection (row 42)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Params reflected into Location / Set-Cookie / custom headers (redirect targets, language, filename in Content-Disposition): %0d%0aSet-Cookie:%20role=admin, %0d%0aX-Debug:1, double CRLF to inject a body; also %E5%98%8A%E5%98%8D unicode CRLF. Then re-request the secondary route with the injected cookie. Parser: injected header in the raw response + proof regex.\"},\n {\"id\":\"ldap-xpath-injection\",\"concept\":\"LDAP / XPath injection (row 43)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Login or directory search over LDAP/XML: `*`, `*)(uid=*))(|(uid=*`, `admin)(&)`; XPath `' or '1'='1`, `'] | //* | //*['`, count()/string-length() oracles bounded to the proof alphabet. Parser: proof regex.\"},\n]\nfor g in new: G[g['id']]=g\norder=['enable-web-prebuild-lane','codify-before-tt','runtime-config-oracle','jwt-session-forge','mfa-step-skip-auth-flow','xxe-payloads','dom-xss-sink-scan','open-redirect-planner','role-tamper-planner','prototype-pollution','websocket-authz','ssrf-filter-bypass','api-shadow-version','nosql-operator-injection','deserialization-gadgets','logic-race-reset','clue-json-router','mastery-concept-dispatcher','recon-crawl-depth2','fetch-metadata-matrix','record-target-responses','stopgate-503-already-solved']\nrest=[k for k in G if k not in order]\nrest.sort(key=lambda k:G[k]['priority'])\nout=[G[k] for k in order+rest]\nassert all(set(g)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'} for g in out)\njs='[\\n'+',\\n'.join('  '+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in out)+'\\n]\\n'\njson.loads(js)\nintro_a=s.index('Priority 1 = plausible',i)\nintro='''Priority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (D19-D27 at ~2-3 lane-days per day). \"prebuild\" = pure python handler\n(request planner + response parser, no I/O; the solver fetches) with offline fixtures = recorded bodies incl. a\ndecoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built (no web prebuild lane, no `web:*` keys in\n.run/prebuild-state.json). Dropped after D13: `ssti-engine-probe`, `port-day22-handlers`. Dropped after D15:\n`ssrf-planner`. Dropped after D18: `cmd-injection-planner` (seen D16 -> `cmd-injection-sequels`),\n`graphql-introspection` (seen D18 -> `graphql-batch-alias-mutation`); `logic-race-reset` narrowed to race/logic\n(reset seen D17 -> `mfa-step-skip-auth-flow`). Added after D18: `runtime-config-oracle`, `mfa-step-skip-auth-flow`,\n`websocket-authz`, `cmd-injection-sequels`, `graphql-batch-alias-mutation`, `crlf-header-injection`,\n`ldap-xpath-injection`; raised to 1: `nosql-operator-injection`, `deserialization-gadgets`, `logic-race-reset`.\n\n'''\ns=s[:intro_a]+intro+'```json\\n'+js+'```\\n'\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(len(out), sum(1 for g in out if g['action']=='prebuild'), [g['id'] for g in out if g['priority']==1])\nEOF\ntail -c 300 reference/coverage/web.md; wc -l reference/coverage/web.md","description":"Update readiness gaps JSON and intro"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3028,"cache_read_input_tokens":106090,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3028},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2f22de87-85c6-4735-9cd3-ecbd50af08de","uuid":"64c47d4b-206b-447b-a6d0-4be3b97b976b","timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:11:51.873Z","request_id":"req_011CgP1cwKg21UmmYfDvW6VS","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01WRuvLqBFbdBzv9MvGq5MW7":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/web.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('## Readiness gaps'); a=s.index('```json',i); b=s.index('```',a+7)\ngaps=json.loads(s[a+7:b])\nG={g['id']:g for g in gaps}\nfor d in ('cmd-injection-planner','graphql-introspection'): G.pop(d)\nG['enable-web-prebuild-lane']['detail']=G['enable-web-prebuild-lane']['detail'].replace('Still true after D15','Still true after D18 (D25 added three more per-day plugins by hand)')\nG['codify-before-tt']['detail']=(\"D16-D18 (cal. 25) repeated it three times at once: singles CORRECT in ~36-40 s at 13:01:01-07Z, codify plugins landed 13:01:08-10Z, TT started 13:01:10Z -> all three TT solver_incomplete (13.8-22 s), hand-solved by live workers in 31-53 s; the D16 plugin was still a `.tmp` when its Mastery ran (3/4 answered, proof-4 hand-solved). Earlier: D09, D10, D12, D13, D15. D11 (plugin before submit) and D14 went first try. \"\n  \"Owner of hctf/ + web skill: for web, gate TT/Mastery start on the codify worker's plugin being importable (or on solver-test pa